comment: Hepatic sinusoidal dilatation can be caused by hepatic venous outflow obstruction or extrahepatic inflammatory conditions; the dilated lumens can appear congested and packed with erythrocytes. Per PMID:15361506 and PMID:29844855, hepatic sinusoidal dilatation is defined as sinusoidal space (lumen) more than one hepatocyte plate in width {xref="https://radiopaedia.org/articles/hepatic-sinusoidal-dilatation", xref="https://tpis.upmc.com/tpislibrary/dlp/Chap11frame.html"}
