def: "failure or abnormality in the formation of the middle of the three primary germ layers of the embryo (the others being ectoderm and endoderm) during gastrulation; mesoderm is the origin of connective tissues, myoblasts, blood, the cardiovascular and lymphatic systems, most of the urogenital system, and the lining of the pericardial, pleural, and peritoneal cavities" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723, https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324]
synonym: "abnormal mesoderm differentiation" EXACT []
xref: GO:0001707
is_a: MP:0001674 ! abnormal germ layer development

[Term]
id: MP:0001683
name: absent mesoderm
alt_id: MP:0001682
def: "absence of the middle of the three primary germ layers of the embryo (the others being ectoderm and endoderm) during gastrulation; mesoderm is the origin of connective tissues, myoblasts, blood, the cardiovascular and lymphatic systems, most of the urogenital system, and the lining of the pericardial, pleural, and peritoneal cavities" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723, https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324]
synonym: "absence of mesoderm" EXACT []
synonym: "Failure of Mesoderm Formation" EXACT []
xref: GO:0001707
is_a: MP:0014141 ! abnormal mesoderm morphology

[Term]
id: MP:0001684
name: abnormal axial mesoderm morphology
def: "failure or abnormality in the formation of part of the middle of the three primary germ layers of the embryo which includes the prechordal mesoderm and the chordamesoderm and gives rise to the prechordal plate and to the notochord" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723, https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324]
is_a: MP:0014141 ! abnormal mesoderm morphology

[Term]
id: MP:0001685
name: abnormal endoderm development
alt_id: MP:0001686
def: "any abnormality in the formation of the innermost of the three primary germ layers of the embryo (the others being mesoderm and ectoderm) during gastrulation; endoderm gives rise to the epithelial lining of the gastrointestinal and respiratory tracts; the parenchyma of the tonsils, the liver, the thymus, the thyroid, the parathyroids, and the pancreas; the epithelial lining of the urinary bladder, urethra, and prostate; and the epithelial lining of the tympanic cavity, tympanic antrum, and auditory tube" [http://discovery.lifemapsc.com/in-vivo-development/endoderm, http://discovery.lifemapsc.com/library/review-of-medical-embryology/chapter-25-germ-layers-and-their-derivatives, http://education-portal.com/academy/lesson/endoderm-layer-definition-derivatives-quiz.html#lesson]
synonym: "abnormal definitive endoderm development" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal endoderm differentiation" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal entoderm development" EXACT []
xref: GO:0001706
is_a: MP:0001674 ! abnormal germ layer development

[Term]
id: MP:0001687
name: thin endoderm
def: "reduced thickness of the innermost germ layer of the embryo" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324, ISBN:0-683-40008-8]
synonym: "thin definitive endoderm" EXACT []
synonym: "thin entoderm" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0014140 ! abnormal endoderm morphology

[Term]
id: MP:0001688
name: abnormal somite development
def: "any anomaly in the formation of mesodermal clusters that are arranged segmentally along the anterior posterior axis of an embryo; somites are transient structures - balls or blocks of paraxial mesoderm cells with an epithelial outer layer and a mesenchymal cell core - that emerge sequentially through a mesenchymal-to-epithelial transition (MET) from the morphologically unpatterned presomitic mesoderm; they give rise to the metameric anatomy of the vertebral column itself, and the associated skin, muscle and tendons" [GO:0001756, PMID:21164524]
subset: IMPC_Prenatal
synonym: "abnormal metablastic segment development" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal somite formation" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal somite segmentation" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal somitogenesis" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0002085 ! abnormal embryonic tissue morphology

[Term]
id: MP:0001689
name: incomplete somite formation
def: "arrest of differentiation or patterning of the somites" [J:62882]
is_a: MP:0009768 ! impaired somite development

[Term]
id: MP:0001690
name: failure of somite differentiation
def: "disorganized or absent somite tissue or somite pattern in development" [J:25248]
is_a: MP:0009768 ! impaired somite development

[Term]
id: MP:0001691
name: abnormal somite shape
def: "anomaly in the characteristic surface outline or contour of mesodermal clusters that are arranged segmentally along the anterior posterior axis of an embryo" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324]
synonym: "irregular somite shape" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0001688 ! abnormal somite development

[Term]
id: MP:0001693
name: failure of primitive streak formation
def: "inability to form the epiblast ridge from which arises the germ layers of the embryo" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324, ISBN:0-683-40008-8]
xref: GO:0007369
is_a: MP:0002230 ! abnormal primitive streak formation

[Term]
id: MP:0001694
name: absent egg cylinders
