[Term]
id: MP:0001700
name: abnormal embryo turning
def: "atypical axial rotation of the germ layers of the embryo during the primitive streak/early somite stage during which the curvature of the entire trunk region is normally reversed and the neural ectoderm moves to the convex region and the midgut region becomes located in the concave region" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324, ISBN:0-12-402035-6]
comment: In mouse, this event occurs at E8.5-E9.5.
subset: IMPC_Prenatal
synonym: "abnormal embryonic axial rotation" EXACT []
synonym: "Abnormal Turning of Embryo" EXACT []
xref: GO:0007669
