[Term]
id: MP:0002346
name: abnormal lymph node secondary follicle morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of a lymph node primary follicle that has undergone antigenic challenge and is characterized by a ring of concentrically packed B lymphocytes surrounding a germinal center, which contains proliferating B cells, and a mantle area that contains nondividing B cells and some helper T cells with macrophages and follicular dendritic cells interspersed" [ISBN:0716749475]
