id: MP:0003897
name: abnormal ST segment duration
def: "anomaly in the length of time between the end of S-wave and the beginning of T-wave; reflects the amount of time the ventricles remain electrically depolarized" [https://orcid.org/0009-0005-7755-8314]
synonym: "abnormal ST interval duration" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0031731 ! abnormal ST segment

[Term]
id: MP:0003898
name: abnormal QRS complex
def: "anomaly in the largest-amplitude portion of the ECG, caused by currents generated when the ventricles depolarize prior to their contraction" [https://orcid.org/0009-0005-7755-8314]
comment: The ventricles have a large muscle mass compared to the atria and so the QRS complex usually has a much larger amplitude than the P-wave.
is_a: MP:0010508 ! abnormal heart electrocardiography waveform feature

[Term]
id: MP:0003899
name: abnormal QT interval
def: "anomaly in the length of time required for ventricular depolarization and repolarization to occur, usually as a result of increased repolarization time, and is measured from the beginning of the QRS complex to the end of the T wave" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4606-0597, PMID:12114851]
comment: A prolonged QT interval is a risk factor for ventricular tachyarrhythmias and sudden death. It varies with heart rate and for clinical relevance requires a correction for this, giving the QTc.
is_a: MP:0010508 ! abnormal heart electrocardiography waveform feature

[Term]
id: MP:0003900
name: shortened QT interval
def: "decrease in the length of time required for ventricular depolarization and repolarization to occur, usually as a result of increased repolarization time, and is measured from the beginning of the QRS complex to the end of the T wave" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4606-0597, PMID:12114851]
synonym: "decreased QT interval" EXACT []
synonym: "reduced QT interval" EXACT []
synonym: "short QT" EXACT []
synonym: "short QT syndrome" RELATED []
is_a: MP:0003899 ! abnormal QT interval

[Term]
id: MP:0003901
name: abnormal PR interval
def: "anomaly in the length of time between the beginning of atrial depolarization and the beginning of ventricular depolarization, measured by the interval from the beginning of the P wave to the beginning of the QRS complex" [https://orcid.org/0009-0005-7755-8314]
comment: The PR interval is measured from the beginning of the P wave to the beginning of the QRS complex. The PR interval reflects the time the electrical impulse takes to travel from the sinus node through the AV node and entering the ventricles. The PR interval is therefore a good estimate of AV node function.
is_a: MP:0006141 ! abnormal atrioventricular node conduction
is_a: MP:0010508 ! abnormal heart electrocardiography waveform feature

