[Term]
id: MP:0004763
name: obsolete absent brainstem auditory evoked potential
def: "absence of the synchronous electrical activity generated by neurons in the ascending auditory system that can be recorded from scalp electrograms by using computer-averaged responses to short tone bursts; by varying frequency, cochlear function can be assessed throughout the hearing range; normally, ABR thresholds vary with frequency, from a sound pressure level (SPL) of 35 dB at 5.6 kHz (a relatively low frequency for a mouse) to 15 dB at 45.2 kHz (a relatively high frequency); each 20 dB corresponds to a tenfold change in amplitude" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "absent ABRs" EXACT []
synonym: "absent BAEP(s)" EXACT []
synonym: "absent brainstem auditory brainstem response(s)" EXACT []
synonym: "absent brainstem evoked responses" EXACT []
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: MP:0011967

[Term]
id: MP:0004764
name: obsolete increased brainstem auditory evoked potential
def: "greater synchronous electrical activity generated by neurons in the ascending auditory system that can be recorded from scalp electrograms by using computer-averaged responses to short tone bursts; by varying frequency, cochlear function can be assessed throughout the hearing range; normally, ABR thresholds vary with frequency, from a sound pressure level (SPL) of 35 dB at 5.6 kHz (a relatively low frequency for a mouse) to 15 dB at 45.2 kHz (a relatively high frequency); each 20 dB corresponds to a tenfold change in amplitude; decreases in auditory thresholds required to generate a response may indicate a increased potential" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "decreased ABR threshold" NARROW []
synonym: "increased ABR amplitude" NARROW []
synonym: "increased ABRs" EXACT []
synonym: "increased BAEP(s)" EXACT []
synonym: "increased brainstem auditory brainstem response(s)" EXACT []
synonym: "increased brainstem evoked responses" EXACT []
is_obsolete: true

[Term]
id: MP:0004765
name: obsolete decreased brainstem auditory evoked potential
def: "reduction in the synchronous electrical activity generated by neurons in the ascending auditory system that can be recorded from scalp electrograms by using computer-averaged responses to short tone bursts; by varying frequency, cochlear function can be assessed throughout the hearing range; normally, ABR thresholds vary with frequency, from a sound pressure level (SPL) of 35 dB at 5.6 kHz (a relatively low frequency for a mouse) to 15 dB at 45.2 kHz (a relatively high frequency); each 20 dB corresponds to a tenfold change in amplitude; increases in auditory thresholds required to generate a response may indicate a decreased potential" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "decreased ABR amplitude" NARROW []
synonym: "decreased ABRs" EXACT []
synonym: "decreased BAEP(s)" EXACT []
synonym: "decreased brainstem auditory brainstem response(s)" EXACT []
synonym: "decreased brainstem evoked responses" EXACT []
synonym: "increased ABR threshold" NARROW []
synonym: "reduced ABRs" EXACT []
synonym: "reduced BAEP(s)" EXACT []
synonym: "reduced brainstem auditory evoked potential" EXACT []
is_obsolete: true

