[Term]
id: MP:0006029
name: abnormal sclerotome morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the group of mesenchymal cells that emerge from the ventromedial part of a somite and migrate toward the notochord; normally, sclerotomal cells from adjacent somites become merged in intersomitically located masses that are the primordia of the centra of the vertebrae" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723, https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4606-0597, ISBN:0803606559]
