[Term]
id: MP:0006110
name: ventricular fibrillation
def: "asynchronous contraction or quivering of individual cardiac muscle fibers in the ventricles" [https://litfl.com/ventricular-fibrillation-vf-ecg-library/, https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4606-0597, NCBI:matt]
comment: Do not confuse with ventricular flutter, a macroreentrant prefibrillatory rhythm that presents as regular, smooth, large-amplitude sinusoidal waves (sine wave pattern), with the ECG often looking identical when viewed upside down. Ventricular fibrillation is characterized by a chaotic, irregular waveform with deflections of varying morphology and amplitude and represents a state of complete electrical disorganization, where the ventricles quiver instead of contracting synchronously, resulting in total loss of cardiac output.
is_a: MP:0006109 ! fibrillation
