[Term]
id: MP:0008836
name: abnormal transforming growth factor beta level
def: "abnormal concentration of a paracrine growth factor that has a potential role in embryonic development, cellular differentiation, hormone secretion, and immune function" [MESH:D12.644.276.374.687]
comment: A factor synthesized in a wide variety of tissues. It acts synergistically with TGF-alpha in inducing phenotypic transformation and can also act as a negative autocrine growth factor. TGF-beta has a potential role in embryonic development, cellular differentiation, hormone secretion, and immune function. TGF-beta is found mostly as homodimer forms of separate gene products TGF-beta1, TGF-beta2 or TGF-beta3. Heterodimers composed of TGF-beta1 and 2 (TGF-beta1.2) or of TGF-beta2 and 3 (TGF-beta2.3) have been isolated. The TGF-beta proteins are synthesized as precursor proteins. (MESH:D12.644.276.374.687).
synonym: "abnormal bone-derived transforming growth factor level" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal milk growth factor level" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal platelet transforming growth factor level" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal TGF-beta level" EXACT []
