[Term]
id: MP:0009363
name: abnormal tertiary ovarian follicle morphology
def: "any structural anomaly in the ovarian follicle in which the primary oocyte attains its full size and is surrounded by an extracellular glycoprotein layer (zona pellucida) that separates it from a peripheral layer of follicular cells permeated by one or more fluid-filled antra; the primary oocyte occupies the cumulus oophorus while the theca of the follicle develops into internal and external layers" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723, UBERON:0000037]
