[Term]
id: MP:0009380
name: abnormal prostate gland ventral lobe morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the rodent prostate lobe that is located below the ventral aspect of the bladder neck" [PMID:12645922, PMID:3308446]
comment: In rodents, the prostate gland consists of three lobes, the anterior prostate (AP; also known as the coagulating gland), the dorsolateral prostate (DLP), and the ventral prostate (VP). These lobes are arranged circumferentially around the urethra and display characteristic patterns of ductal branching and protein secretion (PMID:3308446). In contrast, the adult human prostate lacks discernible lobular organization and, instead, completely envelops the urethra at the base of the bladder (PMID:3308446).
synonym: "abnormal ventral prostate morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal VP morphology" EXACT []
xref: MA:0001740
is_a: MP:0001158 ! abnormal prostate gland morphology

[Term]
id: MP:0009381
name: abnormal prostate gland dorsolateral lobe morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the rodent prostate lobe that lies in the triangular area between urethra and seminal vesicle" [PMID:12645922, PMID:3308446]
comment: In rodents, the prostate gland consists of three lobes, the anterior prostate (AP; also known as the coagulating gland), the dorsolateral prostate (DLP), and the ventral prostate (VP). These lobes are arranged circumferentially around the urethra and display characteristic patterns of ductal branching and protein secretion (PMID:3308446). In contrast, the adult human prostate lacks discernible lobular organization and, instead, completely envelops the urethra at the base of the bladder (PMID:3308446).
synonym: "abnormal DLP morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal dorsolateral prostate morphology" EXACT []
xref: MA:0001739
is_a: MP:0001158 ! abnormal prostate gland morphology

