[Term]
id: MP:0009851
name: abnormal Sertoli cell phagocytosis
def: "altered ability of the Sertoli cells to endocytose and degrade the apoptotic spermatogenic cells and residual bodies (shed cytoplasts) during the maturation phase of spermiogenesis; normally, greater than 50 per cent of differentiating spermatogenic cells undergo apoptosis before maturing into spermatozoa, and these cells are selectively and rapidly eliminated through phagocytosis by Sertoli cells" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
is_a: MP:0001932 ! abnormal spermiogenesis

