[Term]
id: MP:0009943
name: abnormal olfactory bulb periglomerular cell morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the small neuron in the glomerular layer of the olfactory bulb whose dendrites arborize within a glomerulus, where it receives synaptic input from olfactory receptor cell axon terminals, and also engages in dendrodendritic interactions with mitral and tufted cell dendrites; uses both GABA and dopamine as a neurotransmitter" [NLX:nlx_cell_091202]
synonym: "abnormal olfactory bulb periglomerular neuron morphology" EXACT []
