[Term]
id: MP:0009955
name: abnormal olfactory bulb tufted cell morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the principal glutaminergic neuron located in the outer third of the external plexiform layer of the olfactory bulb; a single short primary dendrite traverses the outer external plexiform layer and terminates within an olfactory glomerulus in a tuft of branches, where it receives the input from olfactory receptor neuron axon terminals; axons of the tufted cells transfer information to a number of areas in the brain, including the piriform cortex, entorhinal cortex, olfactory tubercle, and amygdala" [NLX:nifext_121]
xref: NLX:nifext_121 "NeuroLex.org"
