id: MP:0009982
name: abnormal cerebellum globose nucleus morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the two or three small masses of gray matter that is located medial to the emboliform nucleus and lateral to the fastigial nucleus; it receives axons from the intermediate area of the cerebellar hemispheres and its afferents exit through the superior cerebellar peduncle; it is recognized in human cerebellum but is not distinguishable in all mammalian species" [ISBN:0-683-40008-8]
synonym: "abnormal posterior interposed nucleus morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal posterior interpositus nucleus morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0009984 ! abnormal cerebellum interpositus nucleus morphology
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324
created_by: csmith
creation_date: 2010-02-11T10:29:35Z

[Term]
id: MP:0009983
name: abnormal cerebellum fastigial nucleus morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the most medial of the cerebellar nuclei; it receives its afferent input from Purkinje cells of the flocculonodular lobe and the vermis, and most of its efferent connections travel via the inferior cerebellar peduncle to the vestibular nuclei and to the medullary reticular formation" [ISBN:0-683-40008-8]
synonym: "abnormal cerebellum roof nucleus morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal cerebellum tectal nucleus morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal medial cerebellar nucleus morphology" EXACT []
xref: MA:0001009
is_a: MP:0009979 ! abnormal cerebellum deep nucleus morphology
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324
created_by: csmith
creation_date: 2010-02-11T10:30:15Z

[Term]
id: MP:0009984
name: abnormal cerebellum interpositus nucleus morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the nucleus composed of the globose and emboliform nuclei of the cerebellum; in some mammalian species the globose nucleus is not distinguishable" [ISBN:0-683-40008-8]
synonym: "abnormal cerebellum interposed nucleus morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0009979 ! abnormal cerebellum deep nucleus morphology
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324
created_by: csmith
creation_date: 2010-02-11T11:51:12Z

[Term]
id: MP:0009985
name: abnormal inferior cerebellar peduncle morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the paired cerebellar peduncles that connects the medulla spinalis and medulla oblongata with the cerebellum, and is composed of juxtarestiform body and restiform body; it carries many types of input and output fibers that are mainly concerned with integrating proprioceptive sensory input with motor vestibular functions such as balance and posture maintenance" [ISBN:0-683-40008-8]
is_a: MP:0009976 ! abnormal cerebellar peduncle morphology
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324
created_by: csmith
creation_date: 2010-02-11T12:50:42Z

[Term]
id: MP:0009986
name: abnormal middle cerebellar peduncle morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the largest of the three paired cerebellar peduncles; it is composed mainly of afferent fibers that originate within the pontine nuclei as part of the massive corticopontocerebellar tract, whose fibers descend from the sensory and motor areas of the cerebral neocortex, through the pons and into the cerebellar nuclei and cortex" [ISBN:0-683-40008-8]
is_a: MP:0009976 ! abnormal cerebellar peduncle morphology
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324
created_by: csmith
creation_date: 2010-02-11T12:50:42Z

[Term]
id: MP:0009987
name: abnormal superior cerebellar peduncle morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the major output pathway of the cerebellum; most of the efferent fibers originate within the cerebellum dentate nucleus and cerebellum interpositus nuclei, which in turn project to various midbrain structures including the red nucleus, the ventral lateral/ventral anterior nucleus of the thalamus, and the medulla; most of the fibers that pass through this peduncle are involved in pathways important in motor planning" [ISBN:0-683-40008-8]
is_a: MP:0009976 ! abnormal cerebellar peduncle morphology
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324
created_by: csmith
creation_date: 2010-02-11T12:50:42Z

