[Term]
id: MP:0010000
name: abnormal copula pyramidis morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of a part of the cerebellar hemisphere in rodents that corresponds laterally to the pyramis of the vermis of the cerebellum; it is regarded as the homolog of the 'lateral belly' of the the biventer lobule of the human" [http://braininfo.rprc.washington.edu/centraldirectory.aspx?ID=1894, https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/452954/, https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/7541173/, https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/7978337/]
comment: This is a structure present in rodents and is not present in humans. The cerebellum hemisphere structure and lobulation is dramatically different between these species.
synonym: "abnormal COP morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0009963 ! abnormal cerebellum hemisphere lobule morphology
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324
created_by: csmith
creation_date: 2010-02-12T11:19:18Z

