[Term]
id: MP:0010006
name: abnormal flocculus morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the small region of the cerebellum that receives input from the inferior and medial vestibular nuclei and sends fibers back to the vestibular nuclei, and processes and integrates these signals to allow for the constant maintenance of balance" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324, ISBN:0838580343]
comment: This is a structure present in both rodents and humans, but the location and morphology is dramatically different between these species.
