[Term]
id: MP:0010112
name: obsolete abnormal coccygeal vertebrae morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the 3-5 separate or fused bony segments of the coccyx" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324]
comment: In humans and other tailless primates (e.g. great apes), the coccyx is the remnant or a vestigial tail. It consists of 3-5 separate or fused vertebrae (the coccygeal vertebrae) below the sacrum.
synonym: "abnormal coccyx vertebra" EXACT []
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: MP:0002759

