[Term]
id: MP:0010412
name: atrioventricular septal defect
def: "defects in the thin membranous structure between the right atrium and left ventricle that arise from faulty development of the embryonic endocardial cushions; the spectrum ranges from a primum atrial septal defect and cleft mitral valve, known as a partial atrioventricular septal defect (partial AVSD), to defects of both the primum atrial septum and inlet ventricular septum and the presence of a common atrioventricular valve, referred to as complete atrioventricular septal defect (complete AVSD)" [http://emedicine.medscape.com]
comment: The term name is common usage among cardiologists and refers to the specific state in the definition (abnormal communications); do not confuse with parent term.
subset: CvDC_Terms
