[Term]
id: MP:0010413
name: complete atrioventricular septal defect
def: "a type of atrioventricular septal defect in which a single atrioventricular valve annulus, a common atrioventricular valve, and a defect of the inlet ventricular septum are observed; deficiency of the atrioventricular septum also results in the presence of a large primum atrial septal defect" [http://emedicine.medscape.com]
