[Term]
id: MP:0010630
name: abnormal cardiac muscle tissue morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the involuntary muscle comprising the myocardium of the heart and the walls of the pulmonary veins and superior vena cava; cardiac muscle is striated and multinucleate, and the cardiomyocytes branch and are joined to one another via intercalated discs" [ISBN:0-683-40008-8]
comment: Do not confuse cardiac muscle tissue with the myocardium. Myocardium consists primarily of cardiac muscle but these structures are not identical. Cardiac muscle tissue also exists outside the heart so this term has not been made a child of heart myocardial layer directly.
synonym: "abnormal cardiac muscle morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal heart muscle morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "cardiac muscle abnormalities" EXACT []
synonym: "cardiac muscle dysplasia" NARROW []
is_a: MP:0002108 ! abnormal muscle morphology
is_a: MP:0002127 ! abnormal cardiovascular system morphology
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324
creation_date: 2010-10-07T10:28:22Z

