[Term]
id: MP:0010632
name: cardiac muscle necrosis
def: "morphological changes resulting from pathological death of cardiomyocytes or a portion of the cardiac muscle tissue; usually due to irreversible damage" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324]
comment: If necrosis occurs in the heart or any subsection of the heart you should annotate use myocardium necrosis. Cardiac muscle necrosis should be used when the location of the cells is unknown or outside the heart.
synonym: "cardiomyocyte necrosis" EXACT []
synonym: "necrotic cardiac muscle" EXACT []
