[Term]
id: MP:0011113
name: abnormal airway basal cell morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of a long-lived multipotent stem cell of the pseudostratified airway epithelium which is restricted to the tracheal epithelium in mice; airway BCs have been shown to be capable of self renewal, give rise to secretory (Clara) cells and ciliated cells, and play important roles both in epithelial homeostasis and in pathological airway remodeling" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723, PMID:20699479]
is_a: MP:0010942 ! abnormal respiratory epithelium morphology
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324
created_by: csmith
creation_date: 2011-05-11T04:13:01Z

[Term]
id: MP:0011114
name: abnormal airway basal cell differentiation
def: "abnormal or arrest of differentiation of the long-lived multipotent stem cell population of the pseudostratified airway epithelium; changes in the lineage choice of BCs or their undifferentiated daughters might contribute to the mucous cell hyperplasia, metaplasia or squamous metaplasia seen in many respiratory disorders" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723, PMID:17909629]
is_a: MP:0005076 ! abnormal cell differentiation
is_a: MP:0011113 ! abnormal airway basal cell morphology
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324
created_by: csmith
creation_date: 2011-05-11T04:19:42Z

[Term]
id: MP:0011115
name: airway basal cell hyperplasia
def: "increased number of the long-lived multipotent stem cells of the pseudostratified airway epithelium" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "increased airway basal cell number" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0011113 ! abnormal airway basal cell morphology
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324
created_by: csmith
creation_date: 2011-05-11T04:19:42Z

[Term]
id: MP:0011116
name: absent Reichert's membrane
def: "absence of the extraembryonic basement membrane that forms on the inner surface of the trophectoderm during placenta morphogenesis and is secreted by the distal endoderm; normally required for the maternofetal exchange of nutrients and important for postgastrulation development" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
is_a: MP:0003954 ! abnormal Reichert's membrane morphology
