[Term]
id: MP:0011250
name: abdominal situs ambiguus
def: "an abnormality in which the abdominal organs are positioned in such a way with respect to each other and the left-right axis as to be not clearly lateralised and thus have neither the usual, or normal (situs solitus), nor the mirror-imaged (situs inversus) arrangements" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324, PMID:18039396]
