def: "any structural anomaly of the veins that parallel the interlobular arteries, receiving blood from the peritubular capillary plexus and empty into the arcuate veins" [ISBN:0-683-40008-8]
is_a: MP:0011322 ! abnormal kidney cortex vein morphology
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324
created_by: csmith
creation_date: 2011-10-12T02:22:12Z

[Term]
id: MP:0011327
name: abnormal left renal vein morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the longer of the two renal veins that receives blood from the left kidney; the left renal vein usually receives the left inferior phrenic vein, the left suprarenal vein, the left gonadal vein (left testicular vein in males, left ovarian vein in females) and the left second lumbar vein whereas these veins on the right side drain directly into the inferior vena cava" [ISBN:0-683-40008-8]
is_a: MP:0011323 ! abnormal renal vein morphology
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324
created_by: csmith
creation_date: 2011-10-12T02:26:43Z

[Term]
id: MP:0011328
name: abnormal right renal vein morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the shorter of the two renal veins that receives blood from the right kidney; the left renal vein usually receives the left inferior phrenic vein, the left suprarenal vein, the left gonadal vein (left testicular vein in males, left ovarian vein in females) and the left second lumbar vein whereas these veins on the right side drain directly into the inferior vena cava" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324, ISBN:0-683-40008-8]
is_a: MP:0011323 ! abnormal renal vein morphology
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324
