[Term]
id: MP:0011346
name: renal tubule atrophy
def: "acquired diminution of the size of the loops of Henle, the proximal convoluted tubule or the distal convoluted tubule associated with wasting as from death and reabsorption of cells, diminished cellular proliferation, decreased cellular volume, pressure, ischemia, malnutrition, reduced function or malfunction, or hormonal changes" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "atrophic renal tubules" EXACT []
