created_by: csmith
creation_date: 2012-11-30T02:58:33Z

[Term]
id: MP:0011835
name: abnormal urogenital fold morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the pair of folds derived from the cloacal folds which give rise to a portion of the external genitalia; in male embryos they close over the urethral plate and fuse to form the spongy (penile) urethra and ventral aspect of the penis, not including the glans; failure of fusion of the urethral folds leads to hypospadias; in female embryos they fuse only anterior to the anus and form the labia minora" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "abnormal urethral fold morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal urogenital ridge morphology" EXACT []
