creation_date: 2012-11-30T03:20:12Z

[Term]
id: MP:0011837
name: abnormal cloacal membrane morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the membrane that covers the embryonic cloaca, formed by the union of proctodeal (anal pit) ectoderm and cloacal endoderm, with no intervening mesoderm; the urorectal septum joins the cloacal membrane and divides it into an anal membrane and a urogenital membrane; the point where the urorectal septum intersects the cloacal membrane is the future site of the perineal body; proliferation of mesoderm and ectoderm around the cloacal membrane produces primordial tissues of the external genitalia in both sexes: the genital tubercle, genital folds, and genital swellings" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "abnormal membrana cloacalis morphology" RELATED []
is_a: MP:0010115 ! abnormal embryonic cloaca morphology
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324
created_by: csmith
creation_date: 2012-11-30T03:21:45Z

