[Term]
id: MP:0011843
name: abnormal kidney collecting duct epithelium morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the simple cuboidal epithelium lining the lumen of kidney collecting ducts; the mature and differentiated CD epithelium comprises two unique cells types with principal cells responsible for vasopressin-regulated water reabsorption, and intercalated cells regulating acid-base homeostasis; injury to the epithelium is believed to cause epithelial cells to acquire mesenchymal characteristics via epithelial-mesenchymal transition (EMT), a process through which tubular epithelial cells may transform into interstitial fibroblasts and promote renal fibrosis" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
is_a: MP:0004754 ! abnormal kidney collecting duct morphology
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324
created_by: csmith
creation_date: 2012-11-30T03:40:18Z

[Term]
id: MP:0011844
name: kidney collecting duct atrophy
def: "acquired diminution of the size of the kidney collecting ducts associated with wasting as from death and reabsorption of cells, diminished cellular proliferation, decreased cellular volume, pressure, ischemia, malnutrition, reduced function or malfunction, or hormonal changes" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
