[Term]
id: MP:0011855
name: abnormal glomerular filtration barrier morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the highly specialized blood filtration interface that displays a high conductance to small and midsized solutes in plasma but retains relative impermeability to macromolecules; its integrity is maintained by physicochemical and signalling interplay among its three core constituents -- the fenestrated endothelium of the glomerular capillaries, the glomerular basement membrane, and the filtration slits of the visceral epithelial cell (podocyte)" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723, PMCID:PMC2895306]
