[Term]
id: MP:0012126
name: abnormal placenta hemotrichorial membrane morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the three trophoblast cell layers found in rodent placentas between fetal blood vessels and maternal blood sinuses" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
comment: The human placenta is hemomonochorial, as this membrane consists of a single layer of synctiotrophoblast at term. In mice maternal blood bathes a perforated layer of cytotrophoblast cells that overlay two layers of syncytiotrophoblast, thus the murine placenta is hemotrichorial. Maternal blood has direct access to the murine synctiotrophoblast layer I via fenestrations in the murine cytotrophoblast layer.
synonym: "abnormal placenta haemotrichorial barrier" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal placenta haemotrichorial layer" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal placenta haemotrichorial membrane morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal placenta hemotrichorial barrier" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal placenta hemotrichorial layer" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0001711 ! abnormal placenta morphology
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324
created_by: csmith
creation_date: 2013-10-08T14:46:08Z

