[Term]
id: MP:0012233
name: abnormal acidic glycosphingolipid level
def: "anomaly in the amount of any of a subclass of glycosphingolipids that contain large polar heads composed of several sugar units and have one or more of their terminal sugar units bound to a negatively charged molecule at pH 7; negative charges can be provided by sialic acids (gangliosides), uronic acids (uronoglycosphingolipids), sulfates (sulfoglycosphingolipids), phosphates (phosphoglycosphingolipids), and phosphonates (phosphonoglycosphingolipids)" [https://connects.catalyst.harvard.edu/Profiles/display/Concept/Acidic%20Glycosphingolipids, ISBN:9780444527462]
is_a: MP:0020194 ! abnormal glycosphingolipid level
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324
created_by: csmith
creation_date: 2013-11-11T15:07:07Z

[Term]
id: MP:0012234
name: abnormal hepatic diverticulum morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the out-pocket of thickened ventral foregut epithelium adjacent to the developing heart that constitutes the first morphological sign of the embryonic liver" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
comment: In mice, the hepatic diverticulum forms by E9 and expands into an obvious liver bud by E10. The anterior portion of the hepatic diverticulum gives rise to the liver and intrahepatic biliary tree, whereas the posterior portion forms the gall bladder and the extrahepatic bile ducts.
synonym: "abnormal diverticulum hepaticum morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal liver diverticulum morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0003943 ! abnormal hepatobiliary system development
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324
created_by: csmith
creation_date: 2013-11-12T09:45:29Z

[Term]
id: MP:0012235
name: abnormal liver bud morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the liver primordium formed as hepatoblasts delaminate from the anterior portion of the hepatic diverticulum and invade the adjacent septum transversum mesenchyme" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
comment: In the mouse, between E9.5 and E15, the liver bud undergoes significant growth and, following invasion of hematopoietic cells, becomes the primary site of fetal hematopoiesis.
synonym: "abnormal embryological hepatic plate" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal hepatic bud morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal liver primordium morphology" EXACT []
