[Term]
id: MP:0012239
name: abnormal cholangiocyte primary cilium physiology
def: "any functional anomaly of the primary cilia found on the epithelial cells of the bile duct and extending from their apical membrane into the ductal lumen; cholangiocyte cilia respond to mechanical stimuli (i.e. luminal fluid flow) by alterations in intracellular Ca2+ and cAMP and are thought to act as osmosensors that play an important role in ductal bile formation by detecting changes in luminal tonicity and inducing bicarbonate secretion" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723, PMID:18024594]
