name: abnormal circulating antithrombin level
def: "aberrant blood level of the family of glycoproteins which neutralize the ability of thrombin to promote blood coagulation" [ISBN:0-683-40008-8, MPD:Molly]
comment: Six naturally occurring antithrombins have been identified and are designated by Roman numerals I to VI. Of these, Antithrombin I (see FIBRIN) and ANTITHROMBIN III appear to be of major importance.
is_a: MP:0005416 ! abnormal circulating protein level
