name: diastematomyelia
def: "a rare congenital anomaly that results in the splitting of the spinal cord in a longitudinal direction, usually at the level of the upper lumbar vertebra; this condition occurs in the presence of an osseous (bone), cartilaginous or fibrous septum in the central portion of the spinal canal which then produces a complete or incomplete sagittal division of the spinal cord into two hemicords, each half being surrounded by a dural sac; when the split does not reunite distally to the spur, the condition is referred to as a diplomyelia" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "diastomyelia" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0000955 ! abnormal spinal cord morphology
is_a: MP:0005297 ! spina bifida occulta
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324
created_by: csmith
creation_date: 2014-03-20T14:10:17Z

[Term]
id: MP:0012711
name: diplomyelia
def: "true duplication of the spinal cord; each cord has two dorsal and two ventral horns and paired nerve roots, but the two cords are contained within a single dural sac" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
is_a: MP:0000955 ! abnormal spinal cord morphology
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324
created_by: csmith
creation_date: 2014-03-20T14:15:23Z

[Term]
