[Term]
id: MP:0012726
name: abnormal uterine spiral artery morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the corkscrew-like arteries in premenstrual or progestational endometrium; uterine spiral arteries play a vital role in supplying nutrients to the placenta and fetus, and are thus remodeled into highly dilated inelastic vessels by the action of invading trophoblast (physiological change)" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "abnormal coiled artery of the uterus" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal decidual spiral artery morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal endometrial spiral artery morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal maternal spiral artery morphology" EXACT []
