property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324
created_by: csmith
creation_date: 2014-03-21T11:53:50Z

[Term]
id: MP:0012728
name: abnormal somite border morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the anatomical surface separating somites; somite formation requires the physical separation of somitic tissue from the initially continuous presomitic mesoderm (PSM), coalescence of cells in the forming somite, and the establishment of a stable border between the somite and the PSM; when a somite forms in the anterior end of the PSM, an intersomitic boundary (also called a fissure, gap, or cleft) emerges, and it is rapidly followed by a mesenchymal-to-epithelial transition of cells that face a forming gap" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "abnormal inter-somite border morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal intersomitic boundary morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal intersomitic fissure morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal segmental border morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal somite border cell morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal somite boundary morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0001688 ! abnormal somite development
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324
created_by: csmith
creation_date: 2014-03-21T13:33:17Z

[Term]
id: MP:0012729
name: abnormal common carotid artery morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the left or right common carotid arteries which extend headward on each side of the anterior neck and deliver oxygenated nutrient filled blood from the heart to the head, neck and brain; the left originates in the arch of the aorta over the heart; the right originates in the brachiocephalic trunk, the largest branch from the arch of the aorta; each common carotid artery divides into an external and an internal carotid artery" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
is_a: MP:0004181 ! abnormal carotid artery morphology
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324
