[Term]
id: MP:0012752
name: abnormal cardiac neural crest cell migration
def: "any anomaly in the migratory path of cardiac neural crest cells (NCCs), a subpopulation of cranial NCCs which originate from the lower hindbrain between the otic placode and third somite and migrate to the circumpharyngeal ridge (an arc-shape ridge located dorsal to the forming caudal pharyngeal arches) and then into the 3rd, 4th and 6th pharyngeal arches and the cardiac outflow tract (OFT); cardiac NCCs undergo migration away from the neural tube by following a dorsolateral path under the ectoderm, leading them to the pharyngeal arches; after pausing, they resume migration under the pharyngeal endoderm and, along the aortic arch arteries, populate the cardiac OFT where they contribute the aorticopulmonary septum, and ultimately colonize the heart to form the ventricular septum and cardiac ganglia" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
is_a: MP:0002950 ! abnormal neural crest cell migration
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324
created_by: csmith
creation_date: 2014-03-27T16:28:36Z

[Term]
id: MP:0012753
name: increased cardiac neural crest cell apoptosis
def: "increased number of cardiac neural crest cells (NCCs) undergoing programmed cell death" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "increased cardiac NCC apoptosis" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0012744 ! increased neural crest cell apoptosis
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324
created_by: csmith
creation_date: 2014-03-27T16:28:53Z

[Term]
id: MP:0012754
name: abnormal cranial neural crest cell morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the neural crest cells (NCCs) originating in the anterior part of the developing embryo and residing between the mid-diencephalon and the forming hindbrain; cranial NCCs migrate dorsolaterally to form the craniofacial mesenchyme that differentiates into various craniofacial cartilages and bones, cranial neurons, glia, and connective tissues of the face; these cells enter the pharyngeal pouches and arches where they give rise to thymic cells, bones of the middle ear and jaw (mandible), and the odontoblasts of the tooth primordia; like their counterparts in the trunk, cranial NCCs also contribute to the developing peripheral nervous system, along with the pigmented cell (i.e. melanocyte) lineage" [http://discovery.lifemapsc.com/in-vivo-development/neural-crest/cranial-neural-crest, http://embryology.med.unsw.edu.au/embryology/index.php?title=Neural_Crest_Development#Cranial_neural_crest, http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cranial_neural_crest, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "abnormal cephalic NCC morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal cephalic neural crest cell morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal cranial NCC morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal head NCC morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal head neural crest cell morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0009845 ! abnormal neural crest cell morphology
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324
created_by: csmith
creation_date: 2014-04-09T16:02:30Z

