[Term]
id: MP:0013001
name: abnormal enteric neural crest cell morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the neural crest cells that arise predominantly from the vagal region of the neural tube (vagal neural crest), adjacent to somites 1-7 and migrate rostro-caudally along the gastrointestinal tract to form two ganglionated plexuses of neurons and glial cells that comprise the enteric nervous system (ENS); a smaller proportion of ENCCs come from the sacral neural crest, caudal to somite 28, and migrate caudo-rostrally to colonize the distal gut; neural crest cells are termed enteric neural crest-derived cells upon entering the foregut at E9-9.5 in mice (after 4 weeks gestation in humans)" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723, PMID:17514199]
synonym: "abnormal ENCC morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal ENCDC morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal enteric neural crest-derived cell morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0009845 ! abnormal neural crest cell morphology
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324
created_by: csmith
creation_date: 2014-05-06T00:00:00Z

[Term]
id: MP:0013002
name: decreased enteric neural crest cell number
def: "a reduction in the number of neural crest cells that arise predominantly from the vagal region of the neural tube (vagal neural crest), adjacent to somites 1-7 and migrate rostro-caudally along the gastrointestinal tract to form two ganglionated plexuses of neurons and glial cells that comprise the enteric nervous system (ENS); a smaller proportion of ENCCs come from the sacral neural crest, caudal to somite 28, and migrate caudo-rostrally to colonize the distal gut" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723, PMID:17514199]
