property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324
created_by: csmith
creation_date: 2014-05-06T00:00:00Z

[Term]
id: MP:0013010
name: abnormal vagal neural crest cell morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the neural crest cells (NCCs) that arise from the vagal (neck) region of the neural tube (vagal neural crest), adjacent to somites 1-7 (the cranial part of the vagal level overlaps the caudal part of the cranial level, as the first few somites form adjacent to the rhombencephalon, not the spinal cord); the vagal neural crest produces the neurons and glial cells of the enteric nervous system (ENS); like NCCs from other axial levels, the vagal neural crest contributes to the neurons and glial cells of the peripheral nervous system and the melanocytes that populate the skin" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723, PMMID:22016183]
synonym: "abnormal post-otic NCC morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal post-otic neural crest cell morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal vagal NCC morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0009845 ! abnormal neural crest cell morphology
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3691-0324
created_by: csmith
creation_date: 2014-05-06T00:00:00Z

