def: "a herniation of the urinary bladder through an anterior abdominal wall defect; refers to congenital absence of a portion of the lower anterior abdominal wall and the anterior urinary bladder wall, with eversion of the posterior bladder wall through the defect, an open pubic arch, and widely separated ischia connected by a fibrous band" [http://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/exstrophy+of+the+bladder, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723, PMID:17079275]
synonym: "ectopia vesicae" EXACT []
synonym: "everted urinary bladder" EXACT []
synonym: "exposed urinary bladder" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0000538 ! abnormal urinary bladder morphology
is_a: MP:0000757 ! herniated abdominal wall

[Term]
id: MP:0013283
name: failure of ventral body wall closure
def: "failure of the lateral body wall folds (a combination of mesoderm and ectoderm arising on each side of the embryo) to progress ventrally and meet in the midline and/or fuse to close the ventral body wall; normally, this closure is aided by growth of the head and tail folds that cause the embryo to curve into the fetal position and is complete except in the region of the connecting stalk (future umbilical cord); if closure fails, ventral body wall defects occur in the thorax, abdomen, and pelvis and involve the heart (ectopia cordis), abdominal viscera (gastroschisis), and/or urogenital organs (bladder or cloacal exstrophy), depending upon the location and size of the abnormality" [http://www.nbdpn.org/current/2008pdf/AMPresentations/EmbryologySadler.pdf, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723, https://www.inkling.com/read/langmans-medical-embryology-thomas-sadler-12th/chapter-7/ch07-clinical-correlates-01]
synonym: "open ventral body wall" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0003384 ! abnormal ventral body wall morphology

