id: MP:0013447
name: Harderian gland hypertrophy
def: "increase in the bulk size, due to cell enlargement, of the sebaceous gland that is located behind the eyeball and excretes fluid that facilitates movement of the nictitating membrane" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "hypertrophic Harderian gland" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0013446 ! enlarged Harderian gland

[Term]
id: MP:0013448
name: small Harderian gland
def: "decreased size of the sebaceous gland that is located behind the eyeball and excretes fluid that facilitates movement of the nictitating membrane" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "decreased Harderian gland size" EXACT []
synonym: "reduced Harderian gland size" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0013442 ! abnormal Harderian gland size

[Term]
id: MP:0013449
name: abnormal lacrimal lake morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the small cistern-like area of the conjunctiva at the medial angle of the eye, in which the tears collect after bathing the front surface of the eyeball and the conjunctival sac" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "abnormal lacrymal lake morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0008968 ! abnormal lacrimal apparatus morphology

[Term]
id: MP:0013450
name: abnormal lacrimal apparatus physiology
def: "any functional anomaly of the network of orbital structures of the eye that secrete and drain tears from the surface of the eyeball into the nasal cavity; these parts include the lacrimal glands, lacrimal lake, lacrimal ducts, lacrimal canals, lacrimal sacs, nasolacrimal ducts, and lacrimal puncta" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "abnormal apparatus lacrimalis physiology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal lacrimal system physiology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal lacrymal system physiology" EXACT []
synonym: "lacrimal drainage dysfunction" EXACT []
synonym: "lacrymal drainage dysfunction" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0005253 ! abnormal eye physiology

[Term]
id: MP:0013451
name: nasolacrimal duct obstruction
def: "any impediment or blockage of the paired channels leading from the lacrimal sacs to the inferior meatus of the nose, through which tears are conducted through the nasal cavity; may be either congenital or acquired; obstruction of the nasolacrimal duct leads to the excess overflow of tears called epiphora" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "nasolacrimal duct occlusion" EXACT []
synonym: "nasolacrymal duct obstruction" EXACT []
synonym: "nasolacrymal duct occlusion" EXACT []
synonym: "tear-duct blockage" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0008969 ! abnormal nasolacrimal duct morphology

[Term]
id: MP:0013452
