[Term]
id: MP:0013455
name: lacrimal gland atrophy
def: "acquired diminution of the size of any of the paired glands that secrete the aqueous layer of the tear film, associated with wasting as from death and reabsorption of cells, diminished cellular proliferation, decreased cellular volume, pressure, ischemia, malnutrition, reduced function or malfunction, or hormonal changes" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
