[Term]
id: MP:0013464
name: decreased conjunctiva goblet cell number
def: "fewer than normal numbers of the mucin-secreting cells found on the conjunctival epithelium; goblet cell loss has been reported in several inflammatory diseases of the ocular surface, including Stevens-Johnson syndrome, ocular mucous membrane pemphigoid, alkali burn, neutrophilic keratitis, graft-versus-host-disease, and Sjogrens's syndrome" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
