[Term]
id: MP:0013554
name: abnormal apocrine gland morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of any exocrine gland whose cells bud their secretions off through the plasma membrane producing membrane-bound vesicles in the lumen; the apical portion of the secretory cell of the gland pinches off and enters the lumen; it loses part of its cytoplasm in their secretions; apocrine secretion is functional during hormonal stress or puberty; an example of true apocrine glands are mammary glands, responsible for secreting breast milk" [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apocrine, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723, ISBN:0123813611]
