id: MP:0013558
name: abnormal exocrine gland morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of any of the glands of the exocrine system that secrete their essential product by way of a duct to some environment external to itself, either inside the body or on a surface of the body; the duct portion may be branched (compound) or unbranched (simple); the glandular portion may be tubular or acinar, or may be a mix of the two (tubuloacinar or tubuloalveolar); if the glandular portion branches, then the gland is called a branched gland Typical exocrine glands include sweat glands, salivary glands, mammary glands, stomach, liver, pancreas" [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exocrine_gland, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "abnormal duct gland morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal ducted gland morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal glandula exocrine morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0002163 ! abnormal gland morphology

[Term]
id: MP:0013559
name: abnormal exocrine gland physiology
def: "any functional anomaly of any of the glands of the exocrine system that secrete their essential product by way of a duct to some environment external to itself, either inside the body or on a surface of the body; the duct portion may be branched (compound) or unbranched (simple); the glandular portion may be tubular or acinar, or may be a mix of the two (tubuloacinar or tubuloalveolar); if the glandular portion branches, then the gland is called a branched gland Typical exocrine glands include sweat glands, salivary glands, mammary glands, stomach, liver, pancreas" [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exocrine_gland, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "abnormal duct gland physiology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal ducted gland physiology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal glandula exocrine physiology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0002164 ! abnormal gland physiology

[Term]
id: MP:0013560
name: abnormal endocrine gland morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of any of the glands of the endocrine system that secrete their products directly into the circulatory system rather than through a duct" [UBERON:0002368]
synonym: "abnormal ductless gland morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal glandula endocrina morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0002163 ! abnormal gland morphology

[Term]
id: MP:0013561
name: abnormal endocrine gland physiology
def: "any functional anomaly of any of the glands of the endocrine system that secrete their products directly into the circulatory system rather than through a duct" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723, UBERON:0002368]
synonym: "abnormal ductless gland physiology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal glandula endocrina physiology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0002164 ! abnormal gland physiology

[Term]
id: MP:0013562
name: abnormal circumventricular organ morphology
def: "any structural abnormality of any of the secretory or sensory organs located in the brain region around or in relation to the ventricular system that are characterized by extensive vasculature and a lack of a normal blood brain barrier (BBB) and allow for the linkage between the central nervous system and peripheral blood flow; CVOs contain neural tissue and are an integral part of neuroendocrine function; all of the CVOs, besides the subcommissural organ, contain extensive vasculature and fenestrated capillaries which leads to a leaky BBB at the site of the organs; the lack of a BBB allows CVOs to act as an alternative route for peptides and hormones in the neural tissue to the peripheral blood stream, while still protecting it from toxic substances" [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circumventricular_organs, UBERON:0005408]
synonym: "abnormal circumventricular organ of neuraxis morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal CVO morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0002152 ! abnormal brain morphology

[Term]
id: MP:0013563
name: abnormal secretory circumventricular organ morphology
def: "any structural abnormality of any of the circumventricular organs that are responsible for secreting hormones and glycoproteins into the peripheral vascular system using feedback from both the brain environment and external stimuli" [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circumventricular_organs]
synonym: "abnormal secretory CVO morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0000631 ! abnormal neuroendocrine gland morphology
is_a: MP:0013562 ! abnormal circumventricular organ morphology

[Term]
id: MP:0013564
name: abnormal sensory circumventricular organ morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of any of the circumventricular organs that have the ability to sense plasma molecules and then pass that information into other regions of the brain, thereby providing direct information to the autonomic nervous system from systemic circulation" [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circumventricular_organs]
synonym: "abnormal sensory CVO morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0013562 ! abnormal circumventricular organ morphology

[Term]
id: MP:0013565
name: abnormal adrenal gland capsule morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the thick capsule of dense irregular connective tissue that surrounds each adrenal gland and contains scattered elastic fibers; the capsule contains a rich plexus of blood vessels (mainly small arteries) and numerous nerve fibers; some blood vessels and nerves enter the substance of the gland in the trabeculae that extend inward from the capsule and then leave the trabeculae to enter the cortex" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723, ISBN:1581124686]
synonym: "abnormal suprarenal capsule morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0000639 ! abnormal adrenal gland morphology

