synonym: "abnormal PTH secreting cell morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0000678 ! abnormal parathyroid gland morphology

[Term]
id: MP:0013573
name: abnormal parathyroid gland development
def: "aberrant formation or incomplete differentiation of either of the two small, paired endocrine glands, usually found embedded in the connective tissue capsule on the posterior surface of the thyroid gland, which secrete parathyroid hormone (PTH), a hormone that regulates calcium and phosphorous metabolism; in mouse, the parathyroids develop with the thymus from two common parathyroid/thymus primordia originating from the third pharyngeal pouch endoderm; the third pharyngeal pouches are formed at E9.5-E10 and are patterned into dorsal/anterior parathyroid and ventral/posterior thymus domains; the third pouch endoderm proliferates to form bilateral parathyroid/thymus common primordia at E11-E11.5; each primordium separates into one parathyroid gland and one thymus lobe at E12.5-E13.5, which then migrate to their eventual adult locations by about E14.5; in the adult mouse, the parathyroids are located near or embedded within the thyroid gland, and the thymus is situated in the anterior chest cavity" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723, PMID:17382312]
is_a: MP:0000678 ! abnormal parathyroid gland morphology
is_a: MP:0020973 ! abnormal gland development

[Term]
id: MP:0013574
name: ectopic parathyroid gland
def: "a parathyroid gland located outside of its normal position; in the normal adult mouse, the parathyroids are usually found embedded in the connective tissue capsule on the posterior surface of the thyroid gland; because of their common pharyngeal pouch origin, ectopic thyroid and parathyroid tissue can occasionally be found in the thymus" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
is_a: MP:0000678 ! abnormal parathyroid gland morphology

[Term]
id: MP:0013575
name: abnormal forestomach-glandular stomach junction morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the distinct low fold of tissue that separates the non-glandular area of the stomach (forestomach) from the glandular stomach; the limiting ridge extends circumferentially from the large curvature of the stomach to the small curvature, just below the esophagus; at the esophagus, the course of the limiting ridge bends into a U-shape and almost surrounds the esophageal opening" [http://www.google.com/url?sa=t&rct=j&q=&esrc=s&source=web&cd=2&ved=0CCUQFjAB&url=http%3A%2F%2Fjournals.usamvcluj.ro%2Findex.php%2Fveterinary%2Farticle%2Fdownload%2F5889%2F5384&ei=nQ61VJvFEMuQyASZpYGgCw&usg=AFQjCNHtPvbkRJR7v3Jh2Ht2z-s9qVBLGA&bvm=bv.83339334\,d.aWw&cad=rja, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "abnormal forestomach - glandular stomach squamocolumnar junction morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal limiting ridge of stomach morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal margo plicatus morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal squamo-columnar junction between forestomach and glandular stomach morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal squamocolumnar junction with the glandular stomach morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0000470 ! abnormal stomach morphology

