[Term]
id: MP:0013778
name: abnormal mammary gland myoepithelium morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the outer cell layer of the mammary gland epithelium bilayer which is located basal to the luminal (secretory) cells and adjacent to the basement membrane; basal cells (aka myoepithelial cells) are specialized epithelial cells that express smooth muscle-specific contractile and cytoskeletal properties; in lactating females, milk is produced by luminal cells, secreted into the alveolar lumen and collected in the ducts for expulsion out of the body through the nipple, due to the contractile activity of the basal myoepithelial cells" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723, ISBN:8793237073]
synonym: "abnormal mammary epithelium basal cell layer morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal mammary epithelium basal cell morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal mammary MEC morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal mammary myoepithelial cell morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal mammary myoepithelium morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0009504 ! abnormal mammary gland epithelium morphology

[Term]
id: MP:0013779
name: abnormal mammary gland myoepithelium physiology
def: "any functional anomaly of the outer cell layer of the mammary gland epithelium bilayer which is located basal to the luminal (secretory) cells and adjacent to the basement membrane; basal cells (aka myoepithelial cells or MECs) are specialized epithelial cells that express smooth muscle-specific contractile and cytoskeletal properties; during lactation, MECs contract in response to oxytocin to generate the contractile force required for milk ejection; MECs are involved in all developmental stages of mammary gland morphogenesis, modulating proliferation and differentiation of luminal cells; they take part in the formation of extracellular matrix, synthesizing its components and secreting proteinases and their inhibitors; in addition, MECs are regarded as natural cancer suppressors: they secrete suppressor proteins limiting cancer growth, invasiveness, and neoangiogenesis; MECs are markedly resistant to malignant transformation and they are able to suppress the transformation of neighboring luminal cells" [ISBN:8793237073, PMID:20235044]
synonym: "abnormal mammary epithelium basal cell layer physiology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal mammary epithelium basal cell physiology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal mammary MEC physiology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal mammary myoepithelial cell physiology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal mammary myoepithelium physiology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0010172 ! abnormal mammary gland epithelium physiology

[Term]
id: MP:0013780
name: decreased mammary myoepithelial cell contraction
def: "reduced ability of the mammary myoepithelial cells to contract in response to oxytocin and generate the contractile force required for successful milk ejection and lactation" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723, ISBN:8793237073, PMID:20235044]
synonym: "decreased mammary epithelium basal cell contractility" EXACT []
synonym: "decreased mammary epithelium basal cell contraction" EXACT []
synonym: "decreased mammary myoepithelial cell contractility" EXACT []
synonym: "impaired mammary myoepithelial cell contraction" EXACT []
synonym: "reduced mammary epithelium basal cell contractility" EXACT []
synonym: "reduced mammary epithelium basal cell contraction" EXACT []
synonym: "reduced mammary myoepithelial cell contractility" EXACT []
synonym: "reduced mammary myoepithelial cell contraction" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0013779 ! abnormal mammary gland myoepithelium physiology

[Term]
id: MP:0013781
name: abnormal mammary gland luminal epithelium morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the inner cell layer of the mammary epithelium bilayer that lines the luminal surface of mammary gland ducts and alveoli; luminal cells have only limited contact with the underlying basement membrane and surrounding connective tissue; they are secretory epithelial cells characterized by the expression of the receptors for systemic hormones, i.e. estrogens, progesterone and prolactin" [http://umr144.curie.fr/en/research-groups/molecular-mechanisms-mammary-gland-development-marina-glukhova/molecular-mechanisms-, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723, ISBN:8793237073]
is_a: MP:0009504 ! abnormal mammary gland epithelium morphology

[Term]
id: MP:0013782
name: abnormal mammary duct terminal end bud morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the unique club-shaped epithelial structure that develops at the tip of the mammary duct at the onset of puberty (approximately 3 weeks of age in mouse) under the action of circulating hormones; terminal end buds (TEBs) consist of an outer layer of undifferentiated myoepithelial progenitor cells (cap cells), and a multilayered inner core of luminal epithelial cells (body) fated to form the walls of the ductal lumen; both layers have high rates of mitosis, consistent with a motile organ dedicated to ductal morphogenesis; TEBs proliferate, ramify, and actively invade the fad pad to allow the formation of a complex branching structure; this process of branching morphogenesis concludes at about 10-12 weeks of age in mouse, when TEBs have traversed the length of the fat pad and a fully developed ductal tree has formed" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723, PMID:16280048, PMID:16916375, PMID:18296651]
synonym: "abnormal mammary duct TEB morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0009503 ! abnormal mammary gland duct morphology

[Term]
id: MP:0013783
name: absent mammary duct terminal end bud
def: "failure to develop or maintain the unique club-shaped epithelial structure normally formed at the tip of the mammary duct at the onset of puberty (approximately 3 weeks of age in mouse) under the action of circulating hormones; normally, TEBs proliferate, ramify, and actively invade the fad pad to allow the formation of a complex branching structure; this process of branching morphogenesis concludes at about 10-12 weeks of age in mouse, when TEBs have traversed the length of the fat pad and a fully developed ductal tree has formed; absence of TEBs is often associated with reduced ductal outgrowth and impaired branching morphogenesis" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723, PMID:16280048, PMID:16916375, PMID:18296651]
synonym: "absent mammary duct TEB" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0031174 ! decreased mammary duct terminal end bud number

[Term]
id: MP:0013784
name: abnormal mammary gland bud elongation
def: "any anomaly in the process in which a mammary bud grows along its axis; in mouse embryos, the distal end of the mammary bud begins to elongate into the underlying dermal mesenchyme to form a mammary cord (sprout) by E15.5" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723, PMID:25467960]
is_a: MP:0004135 ! abnormal mammary gland embryonic development

[Term]
id: MP:0013785
name: abnormal mammary gland bud morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the morphologically distinct bulb of epithelial cells formed once each mammary placode expands and invaginates into the underlying mesenchyme; in mouse embryos at E12.5, each epithelial bud with its contiguous mesenchyme is elevated above the surrounding ectoderm as a knob or dome; at E13.5, the buds sink into the underlying dermal mesenchyme, and by E14.5 they can no longer be detected externally; in female mouse embryos, five pairs of anlagen or buds are formed along the mammary line between E12.5 and E14.5 by proliferation of basal epidermal cells; while further mammary development is temporarily arrested in females, androgen receptor activation in male embryos causes degeneration of the buds between E13.5 and E15.5; in female mice, further development is resumed at around E15.5 when each bud elongates to form a mammary cord (sprout), invading the underlying fat pad precursor" [http://www.informatics.jax.org/greenbook/frames/frame13.shtml, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723, PMID:12558599]
comment: In male mouse embryos the bud separates from the epidermis by testosterone-dependent mechanisms between E14.5 and E15.5, and subsequently degenerates; male mice have no nipples and usually only four pairs of rudimentary glands consisting of branching ducts with no aveoli, primary ducts, or openings to the exterior.
synonym: "abnormal lactiferous gland bud morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal mammary bud morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal milk bud morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0004135 ! abnormal mammary gland embryonic development

[Term]
id: MP:0013786
name: abnormal mammary gland bud formation
def: "any anomaly in the morphogenetic process in which a distinct bulb of epithelial cells forms from a mammary placode" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723, PMID:20484386]
comment: In mice, as the cells from the placode begin to invaginate into the underlying mesenchyme they pile up at the surface and begin to array themselves in a concentric orientation so that the early bud is elevated above the plane of the surrounding epidermis; as a result, at E12, the developing buds are visible as prominent knobs on the ventral surface of the embryo, which then submerge beneath the plane of the skin; the formation of the epithelial bud is accompanied by dramatic changes in the underlying mesenchyme; cells surrounding the epithelium elongate, condense, and orient their long axis in a radial fashion around the developing epithelial cells; at the end of this process, the mature bud consists of a sphere of concentrically arrayed epithelial cells connected to the skin surface by a stalk of epidermal-like cells; both ball and stalk are, in turn, surrounded by three to five layers of condensed mesenchyme, referred to as the primary mammary mesenchyme; in female mice the mammary buds remain relatively quiescent from E14 to E16, when ductal morphogenesis commences; in male mice, the mesenchyme around the stalk enlarges and condenses further, eventually severing the connection to the skin; this is followed by apoptosis of the mammary mesenchyme and many cells within the epithelial bud as well; consequently, male mice have either no mammary epithelial ducts or only very rudimentary ones.
synonym: "abnormal lactiferous gland bud formation" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal mammary bud formation" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal milk bud formation" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0004135 ! abnormal mammary gland embryonic development

