[Term]
id: MP:0013899
name: abnormal seminal vesicle epithelium morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the pseudostratified columnar epithelium that lines the seminal vesicles and consists of tall, non-ciliated columnar cells and short, rounded basal cells that rest on the basal lamina; polarized columnar cells show features typical of secretory epithelium, including a well-developed Golgi complex, abundant rough endoplasmic reticulum, numerous mitochondria, and apical secretory vesicles; basal cells are the stem cells from which the columnar cells are derived" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723, ISBN:0781767903, ISBN:1455703079]
synonym: "abnormal gonecyst epithelium morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal seminal gland epithelium morphology" EXACT []
