is_a: MP:0013899 ! abnormal seminal vesicle epithelium morphology

[Term]
id: MP:0013901
name: absent female preputial gland
def: "absence of the paired, lobulated, modified sebaceous glands located on the side of the clitoris in female rodents; in contrast to the preputial glands in male rodents, clitoral glands are a minor source of olfactory stimuli contributing to sexual attractivity; unlike other sebaceous glands, they undergo progressive atrophy of the glandular portion with marked ductal ectasia as rodents age; there is no true anatomical equivalent in humans" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "absent clitoral gland" EXACT []
synonym: "absent clitoral glands" EXACT []
synonym: "absent female preputial glands" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0011834 ! abnormal female preputial gland morphology

[Term]
id: MP:0013902
name: abnormal seminal vesicle physiology
def: "any functional anomaly of the sac-like glandular structures situated posterolateral to the urinary bladder in the male and functioning as part of the reproductive system; seminal vesicles secrete a whitish yellow alkaline fluid that constitutes 60-70 percent of the ejaculate in humans; seminal vesicle fluid secretion is androgen-dependent, fructose-rich, and important for semen coagulation, sperm motility, and stability of sperm chromatin and suppression of the immune activity in the female reproductive tract" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "abnormal gonecyst physiology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal seminal gland physiology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0003698 ! abnormal male reproductive system physiology

[Term]
id: MP:0013903
name: abnormal seminal vesicle fluid composition
def: "any alteration in the expected chemical makeup or appearance of the whitish yellow alkaline fluid secreted by the seminal vesicles that constitutes 60-70 percent of the ejaculate in humans; the secretory product of the columnar epithelial cell, which may be seen in the lumen of seminal vesicles, is strongly acidophilic; it contains large amounts of fructose (used by spermatozoa as an energy source for motility) in addition to water, K+ ions, phosphorylcholine, prostaglandins, flavins, citrate, ascorbic acid, and several amino acids and enzymes; seminal vesicle fluid is responsible for coagulation of the ejaculate, can alter sperm motility and capacitation, and acts as an immunosuppressant in the female reproductive tract" [http://www.lab.anhb.uwa.edu.au/mb140/corepages/malerepro/malerepro.htm#LabSeminal, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seminal_vesicle#Function, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723, ISBN:0781767903, ISBN:1455703079]
is_a: MP:0002059 ! abnormal seminal vesicle morphology

[Term]
id: MP:0013904
name: abnormal seminal vesicle muscle layer morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the thick muscular layer of the seminal vesicle consisting of an inner circular and outer longitudinal layer of smooth muscle which contracts during the emission phase of ejaculation to expel seminal vesicle fluid into the prostatic urethra" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "abnormal muscular coat of seminal gland morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal muscular layer of seminal gland morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal seminal vesicle muscular coat morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0002059 ! abnormal seminal vesicle morphology

[Term]
id: MP:0013905
name: preputial gland inflammation
def: "local accumulation of fluid, plasma proteins, and leukocytes in any of the paired, lobulated, modified sebaceous glands located in the inguinal region adjacent to the penis and vagina, with pheromonal functions in male rodents; in males, the preputial gland empties into the preputial cavity and in females, the preputial (aka clitoral) gland duct empties into the clitoral fossa" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "preputial inflammation" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0002254 ! reproductive system inflammation
is_a: MP:0005647 ! abnormal sex gland physiology

