[Term]
id: MP:0013937
name: decreased thyroid gland lobe number
def: "a reduction in the number of the conical shaped sections of the thyroid gland; in most mammals, the thyroid gland consists of two lobes (left and right) connected by an isthmus portion crossing the upper trachea" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723, https://www.jebmh.com/articles/a-comparative-study-of-thyroid-gland-in-some-mammals.pdf.pdf, PMID:28634271]
comment: The thyroid gland varies greatly in different mammals. In dogs and cats, the gland consists of separate masses connected by an isthmus. In horse, paired lobes are highly dissociated but connected by an insubstantial isthmus. In yet other species, the thyroid has a more compact form and exhibits relatively large median (pyramidal) lobe in addition to lateral lobes. This arrangement is found in pigs and human.
