[Term]
id: MP:0014503
name: decreased circulating myoglobin level
def: "decreased blood level of myoglobin, a low molecular weight oxygen binding heme protein that is normally found exclusively in heart and skeletal muscle cells; in blood, myoglobin is bound primarily to plasma globulins, a complex which is filtered by the kidneys; if the plasma concentration exceeds the plasma binding capacity, myoglobin begins to appear in the urine; myoglobin is rapidly released into the bloodstream after muscle damage, and thus can be a useful biomarker in the early phases of heart or skeletal muscle injury" [ISBN:9780124157590]
synonym: "reduced circulating myoglobin level" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0014502 ! decreased circulating protein level
is_a: MP:0031107 ! abnormal circulating myoglobin level
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4606-0597
property_value: terms:date "2024-06-21T20:53:40Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0014504
name: decreased circulating procalcitonin level
def: "reduced concentration in the blood of procalcitonin, a peptide precursor of the hormone calcitonin produced by parafollicular cells (C cells) of the thyroid and by the neuroendocrine cells of the lung and the intestine; the level of procalcitonin is virtually undetectable in the bloodstream of healthy individuals but can rise significantly in systemic bacterial infections and sepsis; it does not rise significantly with viral or non-infectious inflammations" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Procalcitonin]
synonym: "reduced circulating procalcitonin level" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0014502 ! decreased circulating protein level
is_a: MP:0031064 ! abnormal circulating procalcitonin level
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4606-0597
property_value: terms:date "2024-06-21T20:56:49Z" xsd:dateTime

