[Term]
id: MP:0030144
name: abnormal facial muscle physiology
def: "any functional anomaly of any of the striated skeletal muscles innervated by the facial nerve (cranial nerve VII) that, among other things, control facial expression" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
is_a: MP:0002106 ! abnormal muscle physiology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2017-09-18T08:01:14Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030145
name: abnormal digastric anterior belly morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the anterior belly of the digastric muscle which arises from a depression on the inner side of the lower border of the mandible called the digastric fossa, close to the symphysis, and passes downward and backward; the anterior body originates from the first pharyngeal arch and is supplied by the trigeminal via the mylohyoid nerve, a branch of the inferior alveolar nerve, itself a branch of the mandibular division of the trigeminal nerve" []
synonym: "abnormal anterior digastricus morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal digastric muscle anterior belly morphology" EXACT []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digastric_muscle
is_a: MP:0013815 ! abnormal digastric muscle morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2017-09-18T08:34:52Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030146
name: abnormal digastric posterior belly morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the longer, posterior belly of the digastric muscle arising from the mastoid notch which is on the inferior surface of the skull, medial to the mastoid process of the temporal bone; the posterior belly is supplied by the digastric branch of facial nerve" []
synonym: "abnormal caudal digastricus morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal digastric muscle posterior belly morphology" EXACT []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digastric_muscle
is_a: MP:0013815 ! abnormal digastric muscle morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2017-09-18T08:49:22Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030147
name: abnormal digastric muscle physiology
def: "any functional anomaly of the digastric muscle whose action elevates the hyoid when the mandible is fixed and depresses the mandible when the hyoid is fixed; when the two bellies of the digastric contract, they pull upward on the hyoid bone; but if the hyoid is fixed from below, the digastric assists in extreme opening of the mouth such as yawning or taking a large bite" []
synonym: "abnormal digastricus physiology" EXACT []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suprahyoid_muscles
is_a: MP:0030144 ! abnormal facial muscle physiology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2017-09-18T08:56:48Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030148
name: abnormal mylohyoid muscle morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the flat and triangular paired muscle that runs from the mandible to the hyoid bone forming the muscular floor of the oral cavity of the mouth; it is a suprahyoid muscle derived from the first pharyngeal arch that is situated immediately superior to the anterior belly of the digastric muscle" []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mylohyoid_muscle
is_a: MP:0030240 ! abnormal suprahyoid muscle morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2017-09-18T09:47:34Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030149
name: abnormal stylohyoid muscle morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the slender suprahyoid muscle lying anterior and superior of the posterior belly of the digastric muscle; it arises from the styloid process of the temporal bone and inserts into the body of the hyoid bone; it is perforated, near its insertion, by the intermediate tendon of the digastric muscle; the stylohyoid elevates and retracts the hyoid bone, elongating the floor of the mouth during swallowing" []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stylohyoid_muscle
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suprahyoid_muscles
is_a: MP:0030240 ! abnormal suprahyoid muscle morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2017-09-18T10:28:26Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030150
name: absent stylohyoid muscle
def: "absence of the slender suprahyoid muscle lying anterior and superior of the posterior belly of the digastric muscle that elevates and retracts the hyoid bone, elongating the floor of the mouth during swallowing" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stylohyoid_muscle, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suprahyoid_muscles]
is_a: MP:0030149 ! abnormal stylohyoid muscle morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2017-09-18T10:46:31Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030151
name: abnormal buccinator muscle morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the thin quadrilateral muscle occupying the interval between the maxilla and the mandible at the side of the face that forms the anterior part of the cheek or the lateral wall of the oral cavity; it compresses the cheeks against the teeth and is used in acts such as blowing; it is an assistant muscle of mastication and in neonates it is used to suckle" []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buccinator_muscle
is_a: MP:0030039 ! abnormal facial muscle morphology
is_a: MP:0030246 ! abnormal cheek morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2017-09-18T11:59:36Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030152
name: abnormal depressor anguli oris muscle morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the facial muscle that originates from the mandible and inserts into the angle of the mouth; it is innervated by the marginal mandibular branch of the facial nerve and receives its blood supply from the facial artery; the muscle depresses the corners of the mouth which is associated with frowning" []
synonym: "abnormal triangularis muscle morphology" EXACT []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Depressor_anguli_oris_muscle
is_a: MP:0030039 ! abnormal facial muscle morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2017-09-18T12:37:33Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030153
name: dental pulp inflammation
def: "local accumulation of fluid, plasma proteins, and leukocytes in dental pulp tissue; commonly associated with a bacterial infection but can also be due to other insults such as repetitive trauma or in rare cases periodontitis" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pulpitis, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "pulpitis" EXACT []
synonym: "tooth pulp inflammation" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0001846 ! increased inflammatory response
is_a: MP:0031623 ! abnormal tooth physiology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2017-09-21T05:25:53Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030154
name: abnormal tympanic cavity morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the small, air-filled, mucosa-lined cavity that is located in the petrous portion of the temporal bone and houses the auditory ossicles and intratympanic muscles (tensor tympani and stapedius) as well as the chorda tympani and the tympanic plexus of nerves; it is split into two parts: the tympanic cavity proper (the space directly internal to the tympanic membrane) and the epitympanic recess or attic (the space superior to the tympanic membrane)" []
synonym: "abnormal middle ear cavity morphology" EXACT []
xref: http://www.dummies.com/education/science/anatomy/the-anatomy-of-the-middle-ear/
xref: https://radiopaedia.org/articles/middle-ear
xref: https://www.kenhub.com/en/start/c/ear
is_a: MP:0000049 ! abnormal middle ear morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2017-09-21T06:28:32Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030155
name: absent tympanic cavity
def: "absence of the small, air-filled, mucosa-lined cavity that is located in the petrous portion of the temporal bone and houses the auditory ossicles and intratympanic muscles (tensor tympani and stapedius) as well as the chorda tympani and the tympanic plexus of nerves" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "absent middle ear cavity" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0030154 ! abnormal tympanic cavity morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2017-09-21T08:32:14Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030156
name: abnormal tympanic cavity muscle morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of either of the two tiny striated muscles (tensor tympani and stapedius) located within the tympanic cavity; these muscles contract in response to loud noise, inhibiting the vibrations of the malleus, incus and stapes, and reducing the transmission of sound to the inner ear" []
synonym: "abnormal auditory ossicle muscle morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal intratympanic muscle morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal middle ear muscle morphology" EXACT []
xref: http://emedicine.medscape.com/article/874456-overview#a6
xref: http://teachmeanatomy.info/head/organs/ear/middle-ear/
is_a: MP:0000759 ! abnormal skeletal muscle morphology
is_a: MP:0030154 ! abnormal tympanic cavity morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2017-09-21T09:36:12Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030157
name: abnormal stapedius muscle morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the tiny striated muscle found in the pyramidal eminence on the posterior wall of the tympanic cavity, whose tendon inserts onto the neck of the stapes; like the tensor tympani, it helps to dampen loud sounds; it is innervated by a small branch from the facial nerve" []
synonym: "abnormal stapedius morphology" EXACT []
xref: http://www.dummies.com/education/science/anatomy/the-anatomy-of-the-middle-ear/
