[Term]
id: MP:0030159
name: abnormal tensor tympani muscle morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the tiny striated muscle that originates superior to the pharyngotympanic tube, the sphenoid, and the temporal bone and inserts into the handle of the malleus; it tenses the tympanic membrane and dampens the movements of the auditory ossicles to prevent ear damage from loud sounds; it is innervated by the trigeminal nerve" []
synonym: "abnormal tensor tympani morphology" EXACT []
xref: http://www.dummies.com/education/science/anatomy/the-anatomy-of-the-middle-ear/
