[Term]
id: MP:0030199
name: deviated nasal septum
def: "displacement of the nasal septum in which the top of the cartilaginous ridge leans to the left or the right, causing obstruction of the affected nasal passage; normally, the septum lies centrally, and thus the nasal passages are symmetrical" [HP:0004411, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nasal_septum_deviation]
