[Term]
id: MP:0030207
name: absent zygomaticus muscle
def: "absence of the zygomaticus major and minor facial muscles that originate from the body of the zygoma and pass downwards to insert into the corner of the mouth and lateral aspect of the upper lip, respectively" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
