[Term]
id: MP:0030214
name: muscle fasciculation
def: "small, local, involuntary muscle contractions affecting a small number of muscle fibers, often causing a flicker of movement visible under the skin; fasciculations result from increased irritability of an axon (which in turn is often a manifestation of disease of a motor neuron); this leads to sporadic discharges of all the muscle fibers controlled by the axon in isolation from other motor units" [HP:0002380, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "fasciculations" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0009046 ! muscle twitch
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2017-09-28T10:37:25Z" xsd:dateTime

