id: MP:0030217
name: abnormal piriform aperture morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the pear-shaped bony inlet comprising the most anterior and narrowest bony portion of the nasal airway, formed by the nasal and maxillary bones; the maxillary spines mark the inferior margin of the piriform aperture" [https://radiopaedia.org/articles/pyriform-aperture, PMID:17082934]
