[Term]
id: MP:0030232
name: abnormal mandibular canal morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the canal located within the internal aspect of the mandible which contains the inferior alveolar nerve, artery and the vein; it starts at the mandibular foramen, on the lingual side of the ramus, continues on the buccal surface of the body of the mandible, and ends at the mental foramen" [http://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/mandibular+canal, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723, https://radiopaedia.org/articles/mandibular-canal-1]
