[Term]
id: MP:0030240
name: abnormal suprahyoid muscle morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of any of the four muscles located above the hyoid bone in the neck; these muscles include the digastric, stylohyoid, geniohyoid, and mylohyoid muscles and are all pharyngeal muscles, with the exception of the geniohyoid muscle; they have different actions but in general assist in elevating the hyoid bone and widening the esophagus during swallowing" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suprahyoid_muscles]
synonym: "suprahyoid muscle dysplasia" NARROW []
is_a: MP:0002253 ! abnormal pharyngeal muscle morphology
property_value: dc:date "2017-10-03T14:20:37Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723

