property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2017-10-23T10:34:02Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030311
name: abnormal mandibular fossa morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the depression in the temporal bone that articulates with the mandible; it is a part of the temporomandibular joint and lodges the condyle of the mandible; in the temporal bone, the mandibular fossa is bounded anteriorly by the articular tubercle and posteriorly by the tympanic portion of the temporal bone, which separates it from the external acoustic meatus; the fossa is divided into two parts by a narrow slit, the petrotympanic fissure" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mandibular_fossa, https://radiopaedia.org/articles/mandibular-fossa]
is_a: MP:0004423 ! abnormal temporal bone squamous part morphology
is_a: MP:0011210 ! abnormal temporomandibular joint morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2017-10-23T11:42:32Z" xsd:dateTime

