[Term]
id: MP:0030317
name: absent maxillary zygomatic process
def: "absence of the rough triangular eminence situated at the angle of separation of the anterior, zygomatic, and orbital surfaces; in front, it forms part of the anterior surface; behind, it is concave, and forms part of the infratemporal fossa; above, it is rough and serrated for articulation with the zygomatic bone; below, it presents the prominent arched border which marks the division between the anterior and infratemporal surfaces" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zygomatic_process_of_maxilla, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
