property_value: dc:date "2017-10-25T12:19:58Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030320
name: abnormal temporal bone tympanic part morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the curved plate of bone that is situated inferiorly to the squamous part and anteriorly to the mastoid part of the temporal bone; it surrounds the external auditory meatus, forming the anterior wall, floor and some of the posterior wall of the bony external acoustic meatus; its lateral border gives the attachment to the cartilaginous part of the external acoustic meatus; its anteroinferior surface forms the posterior boundary of the mandibular fossa" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tympanic_part_of_the_temporal_bone, https://radiopaedia.org/articles/tympanic-part-of-temporal-bone]
synonym: "abnormal pars tympanica (os temporale) morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal pars tympanica ossis temporalis morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal tympanic bone morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal tympanic plate morphology" EXACT []
