property_value: dc:date "2017-10-25T12:49:24Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030321
name: abnormal tegmen tympani morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the thin plate of bone which separates the middle ear (tympanic) cavity from the dura of the middle cranial fossa and forms the roof of the middle ear cavity; it is formed in part by the petrous portion of the temporal bone, and the squamous portion of the temporal bone" [http://www.drtbalu.com/anat_middleear.html, https://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/tegmen+tympani]
