[Term]
id: MP:0030332
name: accelerated temporomandibular joint osteoarthritis
def: "earlier onset or more rapid progression of a degenerative condition of the temporomandibular joint that results from breakdown of joint cartilage and underlying bone; erosive lesions and joint space narrowing usually indicate acute or early changes, whereas sclerosis, flattening, subchondral cysts, and osteophytes may indicate late changes" [http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2319417016301536, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
