[Term]
id: MP:0030367
name: premature metopic suture closure
def: "early closure of the metopic suture of the skull; premature closure of this suture compromises the transverse growth of both the frontal bones and can cause a narrow, triangular shaped forehead (trigonocephaly) that is associated with orbital hypotelorism" [http://www.skullbaseinstitute.com/craniosynostosis-craniofacial/trigonocephaly.html, PMID:23960302]
comment: In mice and rats, the posterior frontal suture (analogous to the human metopic suture) is the only cranial suture that fuses naturally during the first month of life; fusion proceeds in a defined temporal sequence from an anterior to posterior direction, while all other cranial sutures remain patent throughout the life of the animal {xref="PMID:23300083", xref="PMID:15790973", xref="PMID:8911474"}
synonym: "early fusion of frontal sutures" EXACT []
synonym: "early fusion of interfrontal sutures" EXACT []
synonym: "early fusion of median frontal sutures" EXACT []
synonym: "early fusion of metopic sutures" EXACT []
synonym: "metopic craniosynostosis" EXACT []
synonym: "metopic suture craniosynostosis" EXACT []
synonym: "metopic suture synostosis" EXACT []
synonym: "metopic synostosis" EXACT []
synonym: "premature frontal suture closure" EXACT []
synonym: "premature interfrontal suture closure" EXACT []
synonym: "premature mediofrontal suture closure" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0000081 ! premature cranial suture closure
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2017-11-08T10:55:47Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030368
name: trigonocephaly
def: "presence of a wedge-shaped, or triangular head, with the apex of the triangle at the midline of the forehead and the base of the triangle at the occiput; trigonocephaly can be caused by premature fusion of the metopic suture" [HP:0000243, http://www.skullbaseinstitute.com/craniosynostosis-craniofacial/trigonocephaly.html]
synonym: "triangular cranium shape" EXACT []
synonym: "triangular head shape" BROAD []
