[Term]
id: MP:0030505
name: tooth impaction
def: "cessation of eruption of a tooth caused by a clinically or radiographically detectable physical barrier in the eruption path or by an ectopic position of the tooth; an impacted tooth is one that is unable to fully erupt in its proper location because it is blocked by tissue, bone or another tooth" [https://books.google.com/books?isbn=9350252147, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tooth_impaction]
synonym: "dental impaction" EXACT []
synonym: "impacted teeth" NARROW []
synonym: "impacted tooth" EXACT []
