property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2017-12-22T11:24:57Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030510
name: abnormal tooth placode morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the local thickening that is formed within the primary dental lamina and grows into a solid epithelial tooth bud that invades the underlying mesenchyme; the placodes consist of thickened epithelium and underlying neural crest derived mesenchyme, and they function as the first signaling centers of the tooth" [GO:0060790, https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK27071/, PMID:26755699]
comment: The term placode has not been universally adopted in the field of tooth development research; in mouse, stages prior to bud (E11–E12.5) have often been collectively referred to as the epithelial thickening, dental lamina, or simply initiation stage {xref="PMID:24487243"}
synonym: "abnormal dental anlage morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal dental placode morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal dental primordium morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal odontogenic placode morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal tooth anlage morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal tooth primordium morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0000116 ! abnormal tooth development
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2017-12-22T12:12:26Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030511
name: abnormal dentinoenamel junction morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the interface that joins two distinct calcified tissues, enamel and dentin; it presents a scalloped contour, with its concave side toward the enamel and the convex side toward the dentin, thought to increase adherence of the enamel to the dentin, especially in areas of occlusal stress; DEJ plays a key role in resisting crack propagation from enamel to dentin" [https://books.google.com/books?isbn=1118938313, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dentinoenamel_junction]
synonym: "abnormal amelo-dentinal junction morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal amelodentinal junction morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal DEJ morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal dentin-enamel junction morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal dentino-enamel junction morphology" EXACT []
