property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2017-12-22T12:50:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030512
name: abnormal Tomes' process morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the pyramidal extension at the apical pole of a secretory ameloblast that plays an important role in organizing the enamel crystals into a complex network of rod (prism) and interrod enamel; Tomes' processes interdigitate with the surface of the forming enamel giving it a picket fence appearance and determine the orientation of the newly formed (nucleated) enamel hydroxyapatite crystals; as the secretory stage ends, Tomes' processes are lost and accordingly the last formed layers of enamel are rodless or prismless" [https://books.google.com/books?isbn=0199533016, PMID:20016979]
is_a: MP:0002650 ! abnormal ameloblast morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2017-12-22T13:05:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030513
name: short Tomes' process
def: "decreased length of the pyramidal extension at the apical pole of a secretory ameloblast that plays an important role in organizing the enamel crystals into a complex network of rod (prism) and interrod enamel" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "short Tomes' processes" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0030512 ! abnormal Tomes' process morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2017-12-22T13:17:04Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030514
name: absent Tomes' process
def: "failure to form the pyramidal extension at the apical pole of a secretory ameloblast that plays an important role in organizing the enamel crystals into a complex network of rod (prism) and interrod enamel" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "absent Tomes' processes" EXACT []
