property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2017-12-22T13:19:22Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030515
name: periodontal ligament necrosis
def: "morphological changes resulting from pathological death of periodontal ligament tissue; usually due to irreversible damage" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "necrotic periodontal ligament" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0003668 ! abnormal periodontal ligament morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2017-12-22T13:27:25Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030516
name: abnormal junctional epithelium morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the collar-like band of non-keratinized squamous epithelium that attaches the gingival soft tissue to the tooth surface; the term epithelial attachment refers to the attachment apparatus, i.e. the internal basal lamina and hemidesmosomes, that connects the junctional epithelium (JE) to the tooth surface; in the initiation of periodontitis, JE detaches from the tooth surface and converts gradually, by sprouting laterally and migrating apically, to pathological pocket epithelium" [http://dental.pitt.edu/junctional-epithelium, https://books.google.com/books?isbn=0123977630, PMID:25911094]
is_a: MP:0020460 ! abnormal gum epithelium morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2017-12-22T13:54:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030517
name: detached junctional epithelium
def: "partial or complete detachment of the junctional epithelium from the tooth surface, typically leading to periodontal pocket formation" [https://books.google.com/books?isbn=0123977630]
is_a: MP:0030516 ! abnormal junctional epithelium morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2017-12-22T14:04:20Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030518
name: abnormal outer dental epithelium morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the layer of cuboidal cells located on the periphery of the enamel organ in a developing tooth; this layer is first seen during the bell stage" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Outer_enamel_epithelium]
synonym: "abnormal external dental epithelium morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal external enamel epithelium morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal outer enamel epithelium morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0030508 ! abnormal dental epithelium morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-01-03T09:16:03Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030519
name: abnormal inner dental epithelium morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the inner layer of columnar cells of the enamel organ, located on the rim nearest the dental papilla; this layer is first seen during the cap stage of tooth development, in which inner enamel epithelium cells are pre-ameloblast cells; these will differentiate into ameloblasts which are responsible for secretion of enamel during tooth development" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inner_enamel_epithelium]
synonym: "abnormal inner enamel epithelium morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal internal dental epithelium morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal internal enamel epithelium morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0030508 ! abnormal dental epithelium morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-01-03T09:31:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030520
name: oral mucosa blisters
def: "localized pockets of fluid that form within or beneath the oral mucosa; may appear as pustules, vesicles, or bullae; color varies according to content of blister, which may include blood, serum, mucin, or suppuration" [https://books.google.com/books?isbn=0470673966, https://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/blisterform+oral+lesions]
is_a: MP:0003745 ! abnormal oral mucosa morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-01-03T10:40:18Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030521
name: abnormal cervical loop morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the most cervical part of an enamel organ where the inner enamel epithelium and the outer enamel epithelium merge in a loop, thus delineating the end of the anatomic crown and the site where root formation begins; to form the root region, the cervical loop begins to grow deeper into the surrounding ectomesenchyme of the dental sac, elongating and moving away from the newly completed crown area to enclose more of the dental papilla, forming Hertwig's epithelial root sheath (HERS)" [https://books.google.com/books?isbn=0323290868, https://books.google.com/books?isbn=1455754099, https://www.stembook.org/node/551]
is_a: MP:0030508 ! abnormal dental epithelium morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-01-03T12:00:30Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030522
name: abnormal stellate reticulum morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the network of star-shaped cells found in the core of the dental (enamel) organ between the stratum intermedium and outer enamel epithelium which secrete hydrophilic glycosaminoglycans into the extracellular compartment; the stellate reticulum is most fully developed at the bell stage when intercellular spaces become fluid-filled, presumably related to osmotic effects arising from the high concentration of glycosaminoglycans; the main function of the stellate reticulum is mechanical, protecting the underlying dental tissues against physical disturbance and maintaining tooth shape" [http://dental.pitt.edu/periohistology-glossary, https://pocketdentistry.com/10-early-tooth-development-root-development-including-cementogenesis-and-tooth-eruption/]
is_a: MP:0030521 ! abnormal cervical loop morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-01-03T12:17:21Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030523
name: abnormal stratum intermedium morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the layer of two or three flattened cells located between the inner enamel epithelium and the newly forming cells of the stellate reticulum; it first appears during the early bell stage of tooth development, has a notably high alkaline phosphatase activity, and forms a part of the dental (enamel) organ; this layer, along with the inner enamel epithelium, is responsible for the tooth enamel formation" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stratum_intermedium, https://pocketdentistry.com/10-early-tooth-development-root-development-including-cementogenesis-and-tooth-eruption/]
synonym: "abnormal dental stratum intermedium morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal tooth stratum intermedium morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0010747 ! abnormal enamel organ morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-01-03T12:45:22Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030524
name: abnormal tooth root resorption
def: "pathologic resorption in which cementum or dentin is lost from the root of a tooth owing to cementoclastic or osteoclastic activity in conditions such as trauma of occlusion or neoplasms" [MESH:D012391]
synonym: "abnormal dental root resorption" EXACT []
synonym: "root resorption" BROAD []
synonym: "root resorptions" BROAD []
is_a: MP:0031623 ! abnormal tooth physiology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-01-03T13:09:52Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030525
name: abnormal Hertwig epithelial root sheath morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the bilayered epithelial sheath formed from the fusion of the inner and outer enamel epithelia below the level of the cervical margin of the crown; in mammals, HERS is a transient structure and fragments to form the epithelial cell rests of Malassez; HERS cells appear to be involved in the initiation of the root formation process, in root elongation, and in stimulating both cementogenesis and root dentinogenesis" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Epithelial_root_sheath, PMID:19576204]
synonym: "abnormal epithelial root sheath morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal HERS morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0030493 ! abnormal tooth root morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-01-03T13:45:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030526
name: abnormal enamel cord morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the transient structure of the dental (enamel) organ present at the early cap stage of molar tooth development; the enamel cord is a strand of epithelial cells that runs from (links) the enamel knot to the outer dental epithelial cells, dividing the dental organ into two parts" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enamel_cord, ISBN:978-0-12-597951-1]
synonym: "abnormal dental cord morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal enamel septum morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0010747 ! abnormal enamel organ morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-01-05T12:24:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030527
name: absent enamel cord
def: "missing the transient structure of the dental (enamel) organ that is normally present at the early cap stage of molar tooth development; the enamel cord is a strand of epithelial cells that runs from (links) the enamel knot to the outer dental epithelial cells, dividing the dental organ into two parts" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enamel_cord, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723, ISBN:978-0-12-597951-1]
synonym: "absent dental cord" EXACT []
synonym: "absent enamel septum" EXACT []
