[Term]
id: MP:0030541
name: misaligned incisors
def: "abnormal alignment of the upper and lower incisor teeth, usually resulting in malocclusion; in gnawing rodents, where incisors are rootless and grow continually, signs of incisor malocclusion include uneven wear patterns, sloping of the cutting edges, fractured teeth, altered pigmentation, and obvious pathological overgrowth of the incisors" [HP:0011062, https://books.google.com/books?isbn=0323394302, PMID:19622764]
synonym: "abnormal alignment of incisors" EXACT []
synonym: "crooked incisors" EXACT []
synonym: "incisor misalignment" EXACT []
