[Term]
id: MP:0030542
name: abnormal dentin development
def: "any anomaly in the process whose specific outcome is the formation of dentin, the hard portion of the tooth surrounding the pulp, covered by enamel on the crown and cementum on the root; dentinogenesis begins prior to enamel formation and is initiated by the odontoblasts of the dental pulp; dentin is derived from the dental papilla of the tooth germ; after apposition of predentin and maturation into dentin, the cell bodies of the odontoblasts remain in the pulp inside the tooth, along its outer wall; unlike enamel, dentin continues to form throughout life and can be initiated in response to stimuli, such as tooth decay or attrition" [GO:0097187, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dentin]
synonym: "abnormal dentin formation" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal dentine development" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal dentine formation" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal dentinogenesis" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0000116 ! abnormal tooth development
is_a: MP:0002818 ! abnormal dentin morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-01-19T13:47:52Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030543
name: abnormal predentin morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the initial type I collagen-rich unmineralized extracellular matrix synthesized and secreted by odontoblasts and located at the dentin-pulp interface; predentin is converted to dentin when hydroxyapatite crystals are deposited on the predentin" [https://books.google.com/books?isbn=0470958332]
synonym: "abnormal pre-dentin morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal pre-dentine morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal predentine morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0030542 ! abnormal dentin development
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-01-19T14:15:11Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030544
name: abnormal enamel development
def: "any anomaly in the process whose specific outcome is the formation of dental enamel, the hard outer coating of the exposed portion of the tooth; amelogenesis occurs after the first establishment of dentin, via cells known as ameloblasts, and can generally be divided into two broad stages: (i) a secretory stage that involves proteins and an organic matrix forming a partially mineralized enamel and (ii) a maturation stage which completes enamel mineralization" [GO:0097186, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tooth_enamel]
synonym: "abnormal amelogenesis" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal enamel formation" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0000116 ! abnormal tooth development
is_a: MP:0002576 ! abnormal enamel morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-01-19T14:29:36Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030545
name: abnormal acellular cementum morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the acellular layer of cementum, a living tissue that does not incorporate cells (cementocytes) into its structure, consisting only of extracellular matrix components and mineral; acellular cementum is the first cementum deposited on the dentin of the forming root, and is predominantly found on the cervical/coronal portion of the tooth root; it anchors the primary collagen fibers of the periodontal ligament, providing a strong attachment between the tooth and surrounding alveolar bone" [http://www.7med-pdf.com/1020q/13530-structure-of-cementum.html, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cementum, PMID:27029548]
synonym: "abnormal acellular extrinsic fiber cementum morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal primary cementum morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0003933 ! abnormal cementum morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-01-19T14:53:32Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030546
name: abnormal cellular cementum morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the layer of cementum that contains cementocytes in lacunae; it is most abundant on the apical portion of the tooth root and in the furcation areas of multirooted teeth, and has a role in posteruptive adjustment of tooth position" [http://dental.pitt.edu/periohistology-glossary, http://www.7med-pdf.com/1020q/13530-structure-of-cementum.html, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cementum, PMID:27029548]
synonym: "abnormal cellular intrinsic fiber cementum morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal secondary cementum morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0003933 ! abnormal cementum morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-01-19T15:02:32Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030547
name: abnormal cementum development
def: "any anomaly in the process whose specific outcome is the formation of dental cementum, a bone-like rigid connective tissue covering the root of a tooth" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "abnormal cementogenesis" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal cementum formation" EXACT []
