[Term]
id: MP:0030554
name: abnormal cementocyte morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of an apparently terminally differentiated cementoblast that has become embedded in the cellular cementum in a small cavity called lacuna and that extends long cytoplasmic (dendritic) processes away from the cell body toward other cementocytes and neighboring cells in small channels called canaliculi" [PMID:27029548]
is_a: MP:0008753 ! abnormal osteocyte morphology
is_a: MP:0030549 ! abnormal cementocyte lacunocanalicular system morphology
is_a: MP:0030550 ! abnormal cementoblast morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-01-19T16:40:26Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030555
name: abnormal cementocyte lacuna morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the small cavity within the cellular cementum that is occupied by a cementocyte cell body; cementocyte lacunae are described as larger and more irregular in size and shape (from oval to tubular) and with rougher walls than the typical ellipsoid osteocyte lacunae; occasionally, empty lacunae or lacunae containing more than one cell are observed in cellular cementum, not typically observed in osteocyte lacunae" [PMID:26274352, PMID:27029548]
is_a: MP:0030549 ! abnormal cementocyte lacunocanalicular system morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-01-19T17:02:33Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030556
name: abnormal cementocyte canaliculus morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the slender canals situated between lacunae of the cellular cementum where cementocyte cytoplasmic (dendritic) processes reside; cementocyte canaliculi appear to be less organized, more sparse, and do they radiate outward, with the majority of them oriented toward the vascular periodontal ligament for nutrition, unlike osteocyte canaliculi which are radiating, more dense and arranged in a complex network" [https://books.google.com/books?isbn=8131238016, PMID:27029548]
synonym: "abnormal cementocyte canaliculi morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0030549 ! abnormal cementocyte lacunocanalicular system morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-01-19T17:08:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030557
name: abnormal cementocyte dendritic process morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the long, slender cytoplasmic processes that extend from the cementocyte cell body, run along narrow canaliculi, and are linked to neighboring cementocytes processes via gap junctions; cementocytes harbor fewer dendritic processes than osteocytes" [https://books.google.com/books?isbn=8131238016, PMID:27029548]
synonym: "abnormal cementocyte cytoplasmic process morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal cementocyte dendrite morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal cementocyte process morphology" EXACT []
