[Term]
id: MP:0030566
name: abnormal A band morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the dark-staining region of a sarcomere that is situated between two I bands and marked by partial overlapping of thin (actin) and thick (myosin) filaments; an A band is anisotropic to polarized light and contains the entire length of a single thick filament; its center is traversed by the paler H zone, which in turn contains the M line" [GO:0031672, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sarcomere, https://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/A+band]
synonym: "abnormal A band" BROAD []
