property_value: dc:date "2018-05-10T08:02:41Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030568
name: abnormal H zone morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the relatively pale zone traversing the center of the A band of a sarcomere, visible in relaxed muscle fibers; it consists of the central portion of thick (myosin) filaments that are not overlapped by thin (actin) filaments; within the H zone is a thin dark M line, the attachment site for the thick filaments in the center of the sarcomere" [GO:0031673, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sarcomere]
synonym: "abnormal H band" BROAD []
