property_value: dc:date "2018-09-20T09:18:31Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030788
name: abnormal femur head morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the highest, globular part of the thigh bone which comprises two-thirds of a sphere and articulates with the acetabulum in the pelvic bone forming the hip joint; the head is attached to the femoral body or shaft by the neck of the femur; its surface is smooth, coated with cartilage in the fresh state, except over an ovoid depression, the fovea capitis femoris, which is situated a little below and behind the center of the head, and gives attachment to the ligament of head of femur" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Femoral_head, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Femur, UBERON:0006767]
synonym: "abnormal femoral head morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal head of thigh bone" EXACT [HP:0003368]
