property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-10-03T07:45:26Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030838
name: abnormal acetabular fossa morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the roughened depression in the acetabular floor which extends superiorly from the acetabular notch and hosts the ligamentum teres" [https://radiopaedia.org/articles/acetabulum]
is_a: MP:0004509 ! abnormal pelvic girdle bone morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-10-03T08:17:17Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030839
name: abnormal acetabular notch morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the deep notch (depression) located anteroinferiorly along the margin of the acetabulum; it is bridged by the transverse ligament and thus forms the acetabular foramen through which nutrient vessels and nerves enter the hip joint; the ligamentum teres has part of its origin from the acetabular notch" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acetabular_notch, https://radiopaedia.org/articles/acetabular-notch, UBERON:0014446]
is_a: MP:0004509 ! abnormal pelvic girdle bone morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-10-03T08:36:27Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030840
name: abnormal acetabular labrum morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the horse-shaped fibrocartilaginous structure that attaches to the peripheral rim of the acetabulum, contacts the articular surface of the femoral head, and blends inferiorly with the transverse acetabular ligament; it increases the depth of the acetabulum, increasing static stability and contributes to hydrostatic pressurization of the intra-articular space, joint lubrication, and load distribution" [https://books.google.com/books?isbn=0323549667]
is_a: MP:0030829 ! abnormal hip joint morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-10-03T09:12:31Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030841
name: abnormal transverse acetabular ligament morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the fibrous continuation of the acetabular labrum that is completely collagenous and contains no chondrocytes or cartilage; it consists of strong, flattened fibers which cross the acetabular notch and convert it into the acetabular foramen through which nutrient vessels and nerves enter the hip joint; it prevents inferior displacement of head of femur" [http://www.anatomyexpert.com/app/structure/15415/, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transverse_acetabular_ligament]
is_a: MP:0030829 ! abnormal hip joint morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-10-03T09:36:27Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030842
