id: MP:0030844
name: abnormal pubis body morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the flattened medial portion of the pubic bone entering into the pubic symphysis; superior and inferior rami extend from it; the body forms one-fifth of the acetabulum, contributing by its external surface both to the lunate surface and the acetabular fossa; its internal surface enters into the formation of the wall of the lesser pelvis and gives origin to a portion of the obturator internus" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pubis_(bone), https://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/body+of+pubis]
synonym: "abnormal pubic body morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal pubic bone body morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0004506 ! abnormal pubis morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-10-09T11:10:35Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030845
name: abnormal pubic ramus morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of either of the two bar-like processes (branches or rami) of the pubic bone that extend laterally and posteriorly from the pubic symphysis; the inferior ramus articulates with the ischium; the superior ramus articulates with the ilium and forms the front of the acetabulum" [https://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/pubic+ramus]
is_a: MP:0004506 ! abnormal pubis morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-10-09T11:24:22Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030846
name: abnormal superior pubic ramus morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the bar of bone, triangular in section, which extends posterosuperiorly from the body of the pubis to form the superior boundary of the obturator foramen; it contributes about one fifth of the articular surface of the acetabulum" [https://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/superior+pubic+ramus]
synonym: "abnormal superior branch of the pubic bone morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0030845 ! abnormal pubic ramus morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-10-09T11:30:56Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030847
name: abnormal inferior pubic ramus morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the inferior extension from body of pubic bone that meets with the ramus of the ischium below the obturator foramen to form the ischiopubic ramus" [https://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/inferior+pubic+ramus]
synonym: "abnormal inferior branch of the pubic bone morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0030845 ! abnormal pubic ramus morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-10-09T11:38:05Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030848
name: short ilium
def: "reduced length of the broad, flaring portion of the hip bone, which is distinct at birth, but later fuses with the ischium and the pubis" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "decreased iliac bone length" EXACT []
synonym: "decreased ilium length" EXACT []
synonym: "reduced ilium length" EXACT []
synonym: "shortened ilium" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0005354 ! abnormal ilium morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-10-09T11:53:29Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030849
name: wide ilium
def: "increased width of the broad, flaring portion of the hip bone, which is distinct at birth, but later fuses with the ischium and the pubis" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "increased iliac bone width" EXACT []
synonym: "increased ilium width" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0005354 ! abnormal ilium morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-10-09T11:58:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030850
name: abnormal ilium body morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the thick lower part (base) of the ilium that forms about the upper two-fifths of the acetabulum; its external surface is partly articular, partly non-articular; the articular segment forms part of the lunate surface of the acetabulum, the non-articular portion contributes to the acetabular fossa; the internal surface of the body is part of the wall of the lesser pelvis and gives origin to some fibers of the obturator internus; below, it is continuous with the pelvic surfaces of the ischium and pubis, only a faint line indicating the place of union" [http://www.anatomyexpert.com/app/structure/127/833/, UBERON:0010747]
synonym: "abnormal iliac bone body morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0005354 ! abnormal ilium morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-10-09T12:03:10Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030851
name: abnormal iliac fossa morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the large, smooth, concave surface on the internal surface of the ilium; the fossa is bounded above by the iliac crest, below by the arcuate line, and in front and behind, by the anterior and posterior borders of the ilium; it gives origin to the iliacus muscle" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iliac_fossa]
is_a: MP:0005354 ! abnormal ilium morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-10-09T12:12:02Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030852
name: abnormal ilium wing morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the large, expanded (wing-like) portion of the ilium which bounds the greater pelvis laterally" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wing_of_ilium, UBERON:0010746]
synonym: "abnormal iliac blade morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal ilium ala morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0005354 ! abnormal ilium morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-10-09T12:27:44Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030853
name: abnormal iliac crest morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the superior border of the wing of ilium and the superolateral margin of the greater pelvis; it runs from the anterior superior iliac spine to the posterior superior iliac spine; many of the important abdominal and core muscles are attached to the iliac crest" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iliac_crest, https://www.verywellhealth.com/iliac-crest-definition-3120351]
is_a: MP:0005354 ! abnormal ilium morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-10-09T12:41:49Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030854
name: atlanto-occipital joint dislocation
def: "separation of the joints formed by the occipital condyles and the atlas (C-1)" [https://thejns.org/doi/pdf/10.3171/2012.10.SPINE12430]
is_a: MP:0030795 ! joint dislocation
is_a: MP:0030810 ! abnormal atlanto-occipital joint morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-10-09T13:46:13Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030855
name: abnormal olecranon fossa morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the deep triangular depression on the posterior side of the humerus, superior to the trochlea, in which the summit of the olecranon is received during extension of the forearm" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Olecranon_fossa]
synonym: "abnormal fossa olecrani morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0005296 ! abnormal humerus morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-10-10T10:14:55Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030856
name: abnormal olecranon morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the large bony prominence at the proximal end of the ulna which articulates with the olecranon fossa of the humerus and is palpable at the posterior aspect of the elbow; while the olecranon is an attachment site for several muscle groups including the flexor carpi ulnaris and anconeus, the major muscle attachment is that of the triceps brachii muscle" [https://radiopaedia.org/articles/olecranon, https://www.medicinenet.com/script/main/art.asp?articlekey=9478, https://www.orthopaedicsone.com/display/MSKMed/Olecranon+fractures]
synonym: "abnormal elbow bony tip morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal olecranon process of ulna morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal ulnar process morphology" RELATED []
is_a: MP:0005108 ! abnormal ulna morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-10-10T10:31:48Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030857
name: absent olecranon
def: "missing the large bony prominence at the proximal end of the ulna which articulates with the olecranon fossa of the humerus and is palpable at the posterior aspect of the elbow" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "absent elbow bony tip" EXACT []
synonym: "absent olecranon process of ulna" EXACT []
synonym: "absent ulnar process" RELATED []
is_a: MP:0030856 ! abnormal olecranon morphology
