[Term]
id: MP:0030860
name: patellar dislocation
def: "complete displacement of the patella (kneecap) from its normal position in the patellofemoral groove (trochlea), the V-shaped notch on the front of the femur; the most common direction for a dislocated patella is lateral" [https://www.joionline.net/trending/content/what-recovery-time-dislocated-patella, https://www.stoneclinic.com/patelladislocation]
synonym: "dislocated kneecap" EXACT []
