property_value: dc:date "2018-10-10T12:35:57Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030861
name: abnormal triquetrum morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the bone in the proximal row of the carpus that has a pyramidal shape and that is situated between the lunate and pisiform bones" [https://www.merriam-webster.com/medical/triquetral%20bone]
synonym: "abnormal triangular bone morphology" EXACT []
