[Term]
id: MP:0030865
name: abnormal synovial joint cavity morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the minute space enclosed by the synovial membrane and articular cartilages in a synovial joint; it is the site at which the articulating surfaces of the bones contact each other; it contains synovial fluid, a highly viscous, hyaluronic acid–rich fluid that lubricates the joint surfaces" [https://books.google.com/books?isbn=0803647204, https://opentextbc.ca/anatomyandphysiology/chapter/9-4-synovial-joints/, ISBN:978-0-323-07954-9]
synonym: "abnormal articular cavity morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal joint cavity morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal synovial cavity of joint morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal synovial space morphology" EXACT []
