[Term]
id: MP:0030870
name: abnormal superior horn of thyroid cartilage morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of either of a pair of upward projections from the posterior border of the thyroid cartilage; it is long and narrow, directed upward, backward, and medialward, and ends in a conical extremity, which gives attachment to the lateral hyothyroid ligament" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thyroid_cartilage, UBERON:0011624]
synonym: "abnormal cornu superius cartilaginis thyroideae morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal superior cornu of thyroid cartilage morphology" EXACT []
