[Term]
id: MP:0030871
name: abnormal inferior horn of thyroid cartilage morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of either of a pair of downward projections from the posterior border of the thyroid cartilage; it is short and thick, directed downward, with a slight inclination forward and medialward, and presents, on the medial side of its tip, a small oval articular facet for articulation with the side of the cricoid cartilage" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thyroid_cartilage, UBERON:0011625]
synonym: "abnormal cornu inferius cartilaginis thyroideae morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal inferior cornu of thyroid cartilage morphology" EXACT []
