[Term]
id: MP:0030875
name: abnormal cartilaginous joint morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of any joint that lacks a joint cavity and involves bones that are joined together by either hyaline cartilage or fibrocartilage; there are two main types: synchondroses (or primary cartilaginous joints) where the bones are united by hyaline cartilage, and symphyses (or secondary cartilaginous joints) where the bones are united by a layer of fibrocartilage" [https://opentextbc.ca/anatomyandphysiology/chapter/9-3-cartilaginous-joints/, https://teachmeanatomy.info/the-basics/joints-basic/classification-of-joints/]
is_a: MP:0002932 ! abnormal joint morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-10-17T11:32:38Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030876
name: abnormal costochondral joint morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the hyaline cartilaginous joint (synchondrosis) between each rib and its costal cartilage; the articulation is between the cup-shaped depression in the sternal end of a rib and the lateral end of a costal cartilage; the rib and its cartilage are firmly bound together by the continuity of the periosteum of the rib with the perichondrium of the cartilage; no movement normally occurs at these joints" [https://www.kenhub.com/en/library/anatomy/thoracic-cage, UBERON:0002293]
synonym: "abnormal chondrocostal synchondrosis" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal costo-chondral junction morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal costochondral junction morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal costochondral synchondrosis" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0004053 ! abnormal synchondrosis
is_a: MP:0004625 ! abnormal rib joint morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-10-17T11:59:45Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030877
name: abnormal symphysis morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of any cartilaginous joint in which the articulating bones or cartilages are connected by fibrocartilage; a symphysis is a slightly movable joint (amphiarthrosis)" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Symphysis, UBERON:0002216]
synonym: "abnormal secondary cartilaginous joint morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0030875 ! abnormal cartilaginous joint morphology
is_a: MP:0030878 ! abnormal fibrous joint morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-10-17T12:20:07Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030878
name: abnormal fibrous joint morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of any joint that lacks a joint cavity and involves bones that are joined together by dense fibrous connective tissue, consisting mainly of collagen; most (but not all) fibrous joints are immovable (synarthroses)" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fibrous_joint, https://www.visiblebody.com/learn/skeleton/joints-and-ligaments]
is_a: MP:0002932 ! abnormal joint morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-10-17T12:49:17Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030879
name: abnormal syndesmosis morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of any fibrous joint where the gap between two adjacent bones may be narrow, with the bones joined by ligaments, or the gap may be wide and filled in by a broad sheet of connective tissue called an interosseous membrane; syndemoses are slightly moveable (amphiarthrodial)" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fibrous_joint, https://opentextbc.ca/anatomyandphysiology/chapter/9-2-fibrous-joints/]
synonym: "abnormal syndesmodial joint morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal syndesmotic joint morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0030878 ! abnormal fibrous joint morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-10-17T13:03:59Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030880
name: abnormal infrapatellar fat pad morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the partly adipose wedge-shaped mass formed in the anterior region of the knee that is intracapsular but extrasynovial (and thus extra-articular); it extends superiorly from the patella and alar folds to the tibia and infrapatellar bursa and is delimited anteriorly by the patellar ligament and joint capsule and posteriorly by the synovial membrane" [PMID:25018130]
synonym: "abnormal Hoffa fat pad morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0005334 ! abnormal fat pad morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-10-19T10:38:06Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030881
name: abnormal knee morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the segment of the hindlimb that corresponds to the joint connecting a hindlimb stylopod and zeugopod" [UBERON:0001465]
synonym: "abnormal knee region morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0000556 ! abnormal hindlimb morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-10-19T10:50:54Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0030882
name: abnormal radius head morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the proximal articular surface of the radius that forms part of the elbow joint and that is palpable on the lateral side of the elbow, immediately distal to the lateral epicondyle of the humerus; the radial head articulates with the ulna at the proximal radioulnar joint and with the humerus at the radiohumeral joint; at the proximal radioulnar joint, the radial head sits in the radial notch of the proximal ulna and is held in place by the annular ligaments; at the radiohumeral joint, the radial head sits adjacent to the capitellum of the humerus" [https://radiopaedia.org/articles/radial-head]
synonym: "abnormal caput radii morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal head of radius morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal radial head morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0000552 ! abnormal radius morphology
is_a: MP:0013945 ! abnormal elbow joint morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2018-10-19T11:18:01Z" xsd:dateTime

