id: MP:0031013
name: abnormal egg activation
def: "any anomaly in the series of biochemical and morphological events that converts a metaphase-II-arrested oocyte into a fertilized egg ready to begin embryogenesis; in most mammals, oocyte activation is a spatial-temporal regulated process induced by sperm entry that involves early events such a transient rise in intracellular calcium concentration, cortical granule exocytosis and meiotic cell-cycle resumption, and later events such as pronuclear formation, translation of maternal mRNAs and meiosis-to-mitosis transition" [GO:0007343, https://doi.org/10.1016/J.RBMO.2014.01.008, ISBN:978-0-12-812571-7, PMID:10091064]
synonym: "abnormal oocyte activation" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal ovum activation" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0005410 ! abnormal fertilization
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2020-01-07T11:22:13Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0031014
name: polyspermy
def: "increased incidence of fertilized oocytes fused with two or more sperm due to reduced ability or inability to prevent fertilization by multiple sperm during the egg activation process; normally only a single sperm fuses with the egg plasma membrane and injects its nucleus and other organelles into the egg cytoplasm; if more than one sperm fuses, multipolar or extra mitotic spindles are formed, resulting in faulty segregation of chromosomes during cell division; nondiploid cells are produced, and development usually stops" [ISBN-10:0-8153-4072-9, PMID:16478602]
synonym: "failure of polyspermy block" RELATED []
synonym: "failure of polyspermy prevention" RELATED []
synonym: "polyspermic fertilization" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0031013 ! abnormal egg activation
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2020-01-07T11:47:39Z" xsd:dateTime

