[Term]
id: MP:0031021
name: abnormal gallbladder smooth muscle morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the layer of loose smooth muscle bundles (tunica muscularis) located beneath the mucosa of the gallbladder wall and composed of fibers that are not arranged in distinct layers but lie in circular, longitudinal, and oblique directions; when these fibers contract, the gallbladder’s contents are released through the cystic duct into the bile duct and eventually emptied into the duodenum to aid in the digestion of fats" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gallbladder, https://www.histology.leeds.ac.uk/digestive/gallbladder.php]
is_a: MP:0000767 ! abnormal smooth muscle morphology
is_a: MP:0005084 ! abnormal gallbladder morphology
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: dc:date "2020-02-06T07:58:48Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0031022
name: hepatic megalocytosis
def: "a condition in which hepatocytes exhibit gross enlargement of cytoplasmic and nuclear volume without the formation of mitotic spindles and mitosis, potentially indicating irreversible injury" [https://doi.org/10.1016/B978-0-08-046884-6.01026-5, PMID:11509115, RGD:sjwang]
