property_value: dc:date "2020-05-28T12:41:08Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0031062
name: decreased erythrocyte sedimentation rate
def: "a reduction in the rate at which red blood cells (RBCs) descend under the influence of gravity in a vertical column of anticoagulated whole blood over a period of one hour; a decreased rate may be seen in polycythemia or in certain blood diseases in which RBCs have an irregular or smaller shape that causes slower settling" [HP:0025022, http://www.medicine.mcgill.ca/physio/vlab/bloodlab/esr.htmnerythrocyte]
synonym: "decreased blood sedimentation rate" EXACT []
