[Term]
id: MP:0031064
name: abnormal circulating procalcitonin level
def: "any anomaly in the blood concentration of procalcitonin, a peptide precursor of the hormone calcitonin produced by parafollicular cells (C cells) of the thyroid and by the neuroendocrine cells of the lung and the intestine; the level of procalcitonin is virtually undetectable in the bloodstream of healthy individuals but can rise significantly in systemic bacterial infections and sepsis" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Procalcitonin, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "abnormal circulating PCT level" EXACT []
