[Term]
id: MP:0031065
name: increased circulating procalcitonin level
def: "greater concentration in the blood of procalcitonin, a peptide precursor of the hormone calcitonin produced by parafollicular cells (C cells) of the thyroid and by the neuroendocrine cells of the lung and the intestine; the level of procalcitonin is virtually undetectable in the bloodstream of healthy individuals but can rise significantly in systemic bacterial infections and sepsis; it does not rise significantly with viral or non-infectious inflammations" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Procalcitonin, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "increased circulating PCT level" EXACT []
