[Term]
id: MP:0031089
name: sneezing
def: "a semi-autonomous, convulsive expulsion of air from the lungs through the nose and mouth, usually caused by foreign particles irritating the nasal mucosa; a sneeze expels air forcibly from the mouth and nose in an explosive, audible, spasmodic involuntary action resulting chiefly from irritation of the nasal mucous membrane" [HP:0025095, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sneeze]
