[Term]
id: MP:0031092
name: dysgeusia
def: "a distortion or an alteration in the perception of a tastant; an unpleasant perception may occur when a normally pleasant taste is present, or the perception may occur when no tastant is present" [https://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/dysgeusia]
