[Term]
id: MP:0031097
name: conjunctival chemosis
def: "abnormal swelling (or edema) of the conjunctiva; in chemosis, the integrity of conjunctival capillaries is compromised, leading to increased permeability and leakage of serous fluid; causes include conjunctival irritation, infection, inflammation, trauma, and severe intraorbital inflammation" [HP:0012375, https://link.springer.com/referenceworkentry/10.1007%2F978-3-642-35951-4_765-1]
