[Term]
id: MP:0031123
name: abnormal anterior longitudinal ligament morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the strong, broad fibrous band that covers and connects the anterolateral aspects of the vertebral bodies and intervertebral (IV) discs; this ligament extends from the pelvic surface of the sacrum to the anterior tubercle of vertebra C1 (atlas) and the occipital bone anterior to the foramen magnum; it prevents hyperflexion of the vertebral column, maintaining stability of the joints between the vertebral bodies; it is the only ligament that limits extension; all other ligaments of the vertebral column, like the IV ligaments, limit forms of flexion" [https://www.kenhub.com/en/library/anatomy/joints-and-ligaments-of-the-vertebral-column]
is_a: MP:0004703 ! abnormal vertebral column morphology
is_a: MP:0005504 ! abnormal ligament morphology
