[Term]
id: MP:0031125
name: aspiration pneumonia
def: "pneumonia occurring after abnormal entry of material from the oral cavity or upper gastrointestinal tract into the lungs through the larynx; aspirated material can include saliva, nasopharyngeal secretions, bacteria, liquids, toxic substances, food, or gastric contents; can result in pulmonary complications by way of chemical pneumonitis, bacterial infection, or mechanical obstruction" [HP:0011951, PMID:28879323]
is_a: MP:0001861 ! lung inflammation
property_value: dc:creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
