[Term]
id: MP:0031246
name: abnormal CCL3 level
def: "deviation from the normal levels of CCL3 protein, a chemokine that is secreted by a variety of hematopoietic and non-hematopoietic cells upon stimulation and plays a key role in recruiting inflammatory cells (macrophages, lymphocytes, eosinophils and basophils) to sites of injury or inflammation via the CCR1 or CCR5 receptor; it helps promote wound healing by recruiting macrophages to sites of tissue injury; acts as a potent osteoclast activator and induces bone resorption; exerts HIV-suppressive activity; and inhibits hematopoietic stem cell proliferation" [https://link.springer.com/referenceworkentry/10.1007%2F978-94-007-7696-8_27]
synonym: "abnormal C-C motif chemokine 3 level" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal macrophage inflammatory protein 1-alpha level" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal MIP-1 alpha level" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal MIP-1alpha level" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal MIP1-alpha level" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal MIP1A level" EXACT []
