[Term]
id: MP:0031675
name: abnormal fibrocalcific nodule
def: "presence of one or more nodules (circumscribed, elevated solid lesions) composed of fibrous connective tissue with calcified areas in one or more organs or tissues of the body" [https://joraldiagnosis.com/revista/article/view/234, https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29344473/, https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/3147155/, https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39531891/]
comment: The etiology of fibro-calcified nodules may be related to secondary alterations that result from trauma, infectious and autoimmune diseases or from calcified thrombi. {xref="https://joraldiagnosis.com/revista/article/view/234"}
synonym: "abnormal fibro-calcified nodule" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0005378 ! growth/size/body region phenotype
