[Term]
id: MP:0031676
name: abnormal micronucleus incidence
def: "any anomaly in the number of the small membrane bounded compartments with a DNA content encapsulated by a nuclear envelope and spatially separated from the primary nucleus, occurring in a cell population or tissue in a given time period; micronuclei are typically linked to chromosome instability, genome rearrangements, and mutagenesis" [PMID:33610905]
