[Term]
id: MP:0031679
name: abnormal cell nucleus shape
def: "any anomaly in the characteristic surface outline or contour of the cell nucleus in a cell population, tissue, or organism" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
comment: Nuclear shape depends on the cell type. For instance, human fibroblasts harbor a more or less elongated but often smoothly ovoidal nucleus, whereas several immune cells, such as neutrophils, display a highly irregular lobulated nucleus. Nuclear shape abnormalities are common and can be found in healthy cells and in pathological conditions. {xref="PMID:33662810"}
synonym: "abnormal nucleus shape" BROAD []
is_a: MP:0003111 ! abnormal cell nucleus morphology
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: terms:date "2025-07-28T13:12:19Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0031680
name: decreased cell nucleus size
def: "reduction in the size of the membrane-bounded organelle of eukaryotic cells in which chromosomes are housed and replicated" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723, PMID:25860786]
comment: Do not confuse this term with increased micronucleus incidence MP:0031678. Micronuclei are small membrane bounded compartments with a DNA content encapsulated by a nuclear envelope and spatially separated from the primary nucleus.
synonym: "decreased nucleus size" BROAD []
synonym: "reduced cell nucleus size" EXACT []
synonym: "reduced nucleus size" BROAD []
synonym: "small nucleus" BROAD []
is_a: MP:0014693 ! abnormal cell nucleus size
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: terms:date "2025-07-28T14:09:31Z" xsd:dateTime

