[Term]
id: MP:0031703
name: abnormal interferon type I secretion
def: "anomaly in the production or release of any of the cytokines that bind to the IFN-alpha receptor (IFNAR) complex, a heterodimer of IFNAR1 and IFNAR2 chains, and fulfill key functions in anti-viral immunity" [PMID:15546383, PMID:16681834, PMID:31031767, PR:000025848]
comment: Together with IFN-beta, type I IFNs comprise multiple IFN-alpha subtypes (11 in mice and 13 in humans), IFN-epsilon, IFN-kappa, and IFN-omega in most mammals. In addition, IFN-delta, IFN-zeta (limitin), and IFN-tau have been detected exclusively in pigs, mice, and ruminants, respectively. In addition to being induced in response to viruses, they are also produced in immune responses to other classes of pathogens covering bacteria, parasites, and fungi. {xref="PMID:31031767"}
synonym: "abnormal IFN type I secretion" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal type I IFN secretion" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal type I interferon secretion" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0008555 ! abnormal interferon secretion
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/mgijax/mammalian-phenotype-ontology/issues/4224
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: terms:date "2026-02-18T09:47:11Z" xsd:dateTime

