[Term]
id: MP:0031709
name: ventricular arrhythmia
def: "any type of irregular cardiac rhythm originating within the ventricles of the heart" [https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK537120/, PMID:39252710]
comment: Ventricular arrhythmias are pathologic cardiac rhythms originating from the ventricular myocardium or Purkinje system and can be life-threatening. They include ventricular tachycardia, ventricular fibrillation, premature ventricular contractions (PVCs), and ventricular flutter.
synonym: "ventricular arrhythmias" EXACT []
