[Term]
id: MP:0031712
name: torsade de pointes
def: "a type of polymorphic ventricular tachycardia characterized by oscillatory changes in amplitude of the QRS complexes around the isoelectric line, giving it the name 'twisting of the points'; it is associated with QTc prolongation, which is the heart rate adjusted lengthening of the QT interval, and the rhythm may terminate spontaneously or may degenerate into ventricular fibrillation" [HP:0001664, https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK459388/, https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK532954/]
