id: MP:0031713
name: bidirectional ventricular tachycardia
def: "a rare form of ventricular tachycardia characterized by dual QRS morphologies alternating on a beat-to-beat basis" [HP:0034040, https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK532954/, PMID:35698640]
comment: Bidirectional ventricular tachycardia is typically classified as a polymorphic ventricular tachycardia given that there is more than one QRS morphology, but sometimes it is defined as its own entity as a dual morphology ventricular tachycardia.
