name: prolonged corrected QT interval
def: "increase in the length of time between the onset of the QRS complex (earliest ventricular depolarization) to the end of the T wave (latest ventricular repolarization) corrected for heart rate" [HP:0005184, PMID:24097136, PMID:24827793]
comment: Prolonged QTc can cause premature action potentials during late phase depolarizations thereby leading to ventricular arrhythmias and ventricular fibrillations.
