[Term]
id: MP:0031731
name: abnormal ST segment
def: "any anomaly in the ECG section between the end of the S wave (the J point) and the beginning of the T wave; it represents an electrically neutral area of the complex between ventricular depolarization (QRS complex) and repolarization (T wave)" [https://litfl.com/st-segment-ecg-library/, https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK459364/]
comment: The ST segment is normally flat and at the same level (isoelectric) as the PR and TP segments. It corresponds to the plateau phase (phase 2) of the cardiac action potential during which the ventricular myocardium is refractory to further stimulation.
is_a: MP:0010508 ! abnormal heart electrocardiography waveform feature
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/mgijax/mammalian-phenotype-ontology/issues/4260
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: terms:date "2026-05-04T17:36:28Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0031732
name: ST segment elevation
def: "an upward deviation of the ST segment on an ECG, where the J-point is displaced above the isoelectric baseline" [HP:0012251, https://aclscertification.org/what-is-ecg-st-segment-elevation/, https://ecgwaves.com/st-segment-normal-abnormal-depression-elevation-causes/, https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK459364/]
comment: ST elevation can signal urgent, transmural myocardial ischemia (STEMI). While associated with acute heart attacks, it can also be caused by benign conditions (early repolarization), pericarditis, or ventricular aneurysms.
synonym: "elevated ST segment" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0031731 ! abnormal ST segment
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/mgijax/mammalian-phenotype-ontology/issues/4260
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: terms:date "2026-05-04T17:51:39Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0031733
name: ST segment depression
def: "a downward deviation of the ST segment on an ECG, where the J-point is displaced below the isoelectric baseline" [HP:0012250, https://ecgwaves.com/st-segment-normal-abnormal-depression-elevation-causes/, https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK459364/]
comment: ST segment depression often signifies subendocardial ischemia, especially when horizontal or downsloping. Common causes include myocardial infarction, left ventricular hypertrophy (strain), medications (e.g. digitalis), and hypokalemia.
synonym: "depressed ST segment" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0031731 ! abnormal ST segment
