[Term]
id: MP:0031756
name: first degree atrioventricular block
def: "a delay in the propagation of electrical impulses from the atria to the ventricles characterized by a prolonged PR interval without any dropped beats; every P wave is followed by a QRS complex, i.e., all atrial impulses reach the ventricles" [HP:0011705, https://ecgwaves.com/topic/ecg-first-degree-av-block-i-1-criteria-management/, https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK459147/]
comment: First-degree AV block is more accurately defined as an AV delay because no P waves are blocked. The delay is typically due to a minor AV conduction defect occurring at or below the AV node. In a "marked" first-degree AV block, the PR interval is excessively prolonged and the P waves may be buried in the preceding T wave.
synonym: "1st-degree AV block" EXACT []
synonym: "AV block 1" EXACT []
synonym: "AV block I" EXACT []
synonym: "first-degree atrioventricular block" EXACT []
synonym: "first-degree AV block" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0010519 ! atrioventricular block
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/mgijax/mammalian-phenotype-ontology/issues/4310
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: terms:date "2026-07-20T09:13:22Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0031757
name: second degree atrioventricular block
def: "an intermittent atrioventricular (AV) block with failure of some atrial impulses to conduct to the ventricles, leading to skipped beats; some but not all atrial impulses are conducted through the AV node and trigger ventricular contraction" [HP:0011706, https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK459147/, https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK482359/]
comment: Second-degree AV blocks can be further classified into Mobitz type 1 (Wenckebach) or Mobitz type 2, which can be distinguished by examining the PR interval.
synonym: "2nd-degree AV block" EXACT []
synonym: "second-degree atrioventricular block" EXACT []
synonym: "second-degree AV block" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0010519 ! atrioventricular block
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/mgijax/mammalian-phenotype-ontology/issues/4317
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: terms:date "2026-07-20T12:45:16Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0031758
name: 2:1 atrioventricular block
def: "a type of second-degree atrioventricular (AV) block in which every other P wave is not conducted through the AV node such that only every other P wave is followed by a QRS complex" [HP:0034305, https://litfl.com/av-block-2nd-degree-fixed-ratio-blocks/, https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK459147/]
comment: When every other P wave is blocked (not conducted), it is impossible to differentiate between Mobitz type I (Wenckebach) and Mobitz type II AV block, so this entity is called a 2:1 AV block.
synonym: "2:1 AV block" EXACT []
synonym: "second-degree 2:1 AV block" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0031757 ! second degree atrioventricular block
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/mgijax/mammalian-phenotype-ontology/issues/4317
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: terms:date "2026-07-20T12:51:18Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0031759
name: high degree atrioventricular block
def: "an advanced form of second-degree atrioventricular (AV) block characterized by the presence of 2 or more consecutive, non-conducted P waves occurring at a constant physiologic rate, along with evidence of AV conduction; the P-to-QRS ratio is 3:1 or greater, producing an extremely slow ventricular rate" [https://litfl.com/av-block-2nd-degree-high-grade-av-block/, https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK459147/]
comment: High-grade AV block may result from either Mobitz I or Mobitz II AV block. High-grade AV block and Mobitz II are considered pathological and frequently progress to a complete (third-degree) heart block.
synonym: "2nd degree, high-grade AV block" EXACT []
synonym: "high-degree atrioventricular block" EXACT []
synonym: "high-degree AV block" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0031757 ! second degree atrioventricular block
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/mgijax/mammalian-phenotype-ontology/issues/4317
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: terms:date "2026-07-20T13:00:23Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0031760
name: Mobitz I atrioventricular block
def: "a type of second-degree atrioventricular block characterized by P waves exhibiting a consistent rate and a gradual prolongation of the PR interval; this is followed by periodic occurrences of single non-conducted P waves, typically accompanied by P waves preceding and following the non-conducted P waves" [HP:0011707, https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK459147/, https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK482359/]
comment: Mobitz I is usually due to reversible conduction block at the level of the AV node. It is usually a benign rhythm, causing minimal hemodynamic disturbance and with low risk of progression to third-degree heart block.
synonym: "2nd-degree, Mobitz I AV block" EXACT []
synonym: "Mobitz I AV block" EXACT []
synonym: "Mobitz type 1 atrioventricular block" EXACT []
synonym: "Mobitz type I second-degree AV block" EXACT []
synonym: "Wenckebach block" EXACT []
synonym: "Wenckebach phenomenon" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0031757 ! second degree atrioventricular block
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/mgijax/mammalian-phenotype-ontology/issues/4317
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: terms:date "2026-07-20T13:04:51Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0031761
name: Mobitz II atrioventricular block
def: "a more severe type of second-degree atrioventricular block characterized by P waves occurring at a constant rate and periodic single non-conducted P waves that arise at unpredictable intervals; these non-conducted P waves are typically observed alongside other P waves, both before and after the non-conducted P wave, and exhibit consistent PR intervals" [HP:0011708, https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK459147/, https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK482359/]
comment: Unlike Mobitz I (which usually occurs in the AV node and is often benign), Mobitz II is typically caused by structural damage in the His-Purkinje system below the AV node and often progresses to complete (third-degree) AV block.
synonym: "2nd-degree, Mobitz II AV block" EXACT []
synonym: "Hay block" EXACT []
synonym: "Mobitz II AV block" EXACT []
synonym: "Mobitz type 2 atrioventricular block" EXACT []
synonym: "Mobitz type II second-degree AV block" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0031757 ! second degree atrioventricular block
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/mgijax/mammalian-phenotype-ontology/issues/4317
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: terms:date "2026-07-20T13:17:03Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:0031762
name: third degree atrioventricular block
def: "a life-threatening atrioventricular (AV) block characterized by complete AV dissociation, with no supraventricular impulses conducted to the ventricles; ECG demonstrates more P waves than QRS complexes, a highly variable PR interval, and independent atrial and ventricular rates" [HP:0001709, https://litfl.com/av-block-3rd-degree-complete-heart-block/, https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK459147/]
comment: In third-degree AV block, there is no relationship between P waves and QRS complexes. The P waves are said to “march through” the QRS complexes at their regular, faster rate. The QRS complexes also occur at a regular but slower rate. Two independent rhythms occur simultaneously. Ventricular activity is maintained by a subsidiary pacemaker, either a junctional escape rhythm (narrow QRS complex) or a ventricular escape rhythm (wide QRS complex).
synonym: "3rd-degree AV block" EXACT []
synonym: "complete heart block" EXACT []
synonym: "third-degree atrioventricular block" EXACT []
synonym: "third-degree heart block" RELATED []
is_a: MP:0010519 ! atrioventricular block
property_value: IAO:0000233 https://github.com/mgijax/mammalian-phenotype-ontology/issues/4318
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723
property_value: terms:date "2026-07-20T14:30:31Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: MP:3000001
name: abnormal gastrula morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the pear shaped trilaminar embryonic stage in which the primititve streak elongates, the epiblast cells migrate medially towards the streak, enter the primitive groove and migrate laterally to organize into the intraembryonic mesoderm (epithelio-mesenchymal transition) between the embryonic ectoderm and primitive endoderm; the notochordal process forms and extends, and the disc becomes pear shaped as the notochordal process grows" [http://discovery.lifemapsc.com/library/review-of-medical-embryology/chapter-18-week-3-of-development-trilaminar-germ-disk-embryo-formation-and-gastrulation]
synonym: "abnormal trilaminar blastocyst morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal trilaminar disc morphology" RELATED []
synonym: "abnormal trilaminar disk morphology" RELATED []
synonym: "abnormal trilaminar embryonic disc morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal trilaminar embryonic disk morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal trilaminar germ disc morphology" EXACT []
