[Term]
id: MP:3000003
name: abnormal Ebner's gland morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the serous salivary glands which reside adjacent to the moats surrounding the circumvallate and foliate papillae just anterior to the posterior third of the tongue, anterior to the terminal sulcus; these exocrine glands secrete lingual lipase initiating the process of lipid hydrolysis in the mouth and empty their serous secretion into the base of the moats around the foliate and circumvallate papillae; their secretion presumably flushes material from the moat to enable the taste buds to respond rapidly to changing stimuli." [GOC:TermGenie, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "abnormal gustatory gland morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal Von Ebner's gland morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "posterior deep lingual gland" EXACT []
synonym: "posterior lingual serous gland" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0003791 ! abnormal minor salivary gland morphology
is_a: MP:0008052 ! abnormal serous gland morphology
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4606-0597
created_by: csmith
creation_date: 2014-12-04T20:40:06Z

[Term]
id: MP:3000004
name: abnormal nictitating membrane morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the translucent fold of the mucous membrane of the conjunctiva present in some animals that can be drawn across the eye for protection and to moisten it while maintaining visibility; in many mammals, a small, vestigial portion of the membrane remains in the corner of the eye; in mice, the nictitating membrane is very small and composed of a very thin core of cartilage covered by loose connective tissue" [GOC:TermGenie, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "abnormal nictitans morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal palperbra tertia morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal third eyelid morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0001340 ! abnormal eyelid morphology
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4606-0597
created_by: csmith
creation_date: 2014-12-04T20:44:25Z

[Term]
id: MP:3000005
name: abnormal lacrimal sac morphology
def: "any structural anomaly of the upper dilated end of the nasolacrimal duct that is lodged in a deep groove formed by the lacrimal bone and frontal process of the maxilla; it connects the lacrimal canaliculi, which drain tears from the eye's surface, and the nasolacrimal duct, which conveys this fluid into the nasal cavity; like the nasolacrimal duct, the sac is lined by stratified columnar epithelium with mucus-secreting goblet cells, and is surrounded by connective tissue" [GOC:TermGenie, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6490-7723]
synonym: "abnormal lacrymal sac morphology" EXACT []
synonym: "abnormal saccus lacrimalis morphology" EXACT []
is_a: MP:0001346 ! abnormal lacrimal gland morphology
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4606-0597
created_by: csmith
creation_date: 2014-12-04T20:44:33Z

